necessary. Makes copies of supplementary materials for distribution in class. Evaluate and provide records of Student Outcomes for accreditation purposes. Please note that this pool is open for the 2025-2026 academic year and is reviewed based on departmental needs. Screening of applications will occur as positions become available and continue until positions are filled. Qualified candidates are encouraged to apply to Job Opening ID 536092 at careers.fiu.edu and attach their CV. This pool will remain open until October 31st, 2026. Minimum Qualifications Primary Instructors Master's Degree in Engineering, Architecture, Construction Management, Information Sciences or a related field Prior teaching experience at the university level, either as a teaching assistant or a graduate research assistant. Secondary Instructors and Course Assistants Bachelor's Degree in Information Sciences Engineering, Architecture, Construction Management, or a related field. Desired Qualifications Has a comprehensive grasp on his or her particular area of academic study. Demonstrates excellent written and verbal communication skills. Exhibits a commitment to promoting academic excellence in students. Has the ability to solve problems and assess results. Demonstrates a high level of self-discipline and self-motivation. Exudes a positive, supportive, and cooperative disposition toward others. Is punctual and detail-oriented with a demonstrated ability to perform assigned tasks. Job Category Adjunct Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an 