      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer in Chemistry & Biochemistry",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2025-11-01 Department: Chemistry College: College of Arts, Sciences and Education Job family: Adjunct Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Information The Department of Chemistry at Florida International University is seeking adjunct instructors to teach courses offered within the department curriculum. Duties include but are not limited to: Utilizes Canvas Learning Management System (LMS) for use in communication, assignments, and grading if applicable. Attends training for Canvas LMS, if necessary. Coordinates coursework with Supervisor, Program Leader, Discipline Lead, and/or Department Chair. Maintains records of attendance, involvement, and progress through Canvas LMS if applicable. Facilitates class instruction and assigned class content in accordance with the Learning Objectives that are developed by the Department. Responds to students and Departmental correspondence promptly. Communicates with students outside of class to provide supplementary instruction, when necessary. Please note that this pool is open for the 2025-2026 academic year and is reviewed based on departmental needs. Screening of applications will occur as positions become available and continue until positions are filled. Qualified candidates are encouraged to apply to Job Opening ID 536107 at careers.fiu.edu and attach their CV. This pool will remain open until October 31st, 2026. Minimum Qualifications Primary Instructor: Master's Degree in Chemistry or Biochemistry or equivalent. Secondary Instructor, Course Assistant and Other Instructional: Bachelor's Degree in Chemistry or Biochemistry or equivalent. Job Category Adjunct Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \".