      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer in Architecture, Studio",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2025-11-01 Department: Architecture College: College of Communication, Architecture and the Arts Job family: Adjunct Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Information The Department of Architecture at Florida International University is seeking adjunct instructors to teach in the lower or upper division design studio sequence of a NAAB accredited Master of Architecture Program. Instructors are expected to hold 2 hours a week of office hours. Design studio instructors teach in coordinated studios with other faculty or individually. Each instructor oversees a studio section of approximately 12-18 students. Instructors meet with students in an open studio at the FIU Paul L. Cejas School of Architecture Building (PCA) or at the FIU Miami Beach Urban Studio (MBUS). Instructors are expected to guide the design work of each student with critiques, sketches, lectures and group reviews. Please note that this pool is open for the 2025-2026 academic year and is reviewed based on departmental needs. Screening of applications will occur as positions become availab