ls with disabilities and veterans. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment decisions, programs, and events without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, or protected veteran status. For inquiries regarding non-discrimination, contact FIU's Office of Civil Rights at 305.348.2785 or email ocr@fiu.edu. Reasonable Accommodation Statement Should you need an ADA accommodation to participate in a University event, program, or activity or need to request materials in an accessible format, please contact FIU's Office of Civil Rights (OCR) at 305-348-2785 or accommodations@fiu.edu. All requests for ADA accommodation or accessible materials for this event must be submitted to OCR at least seven (7) business days prior to the event or at the earliest possible opportunity. Desired Qualifications Documented professional experience in location-based entertainment (LBE) industries such as: Sports: Sports communication, fan engagement, stadium or arena-based entertainment, sponsorship/partnership development. Music: Music marketing, live events, festival/venue management, digital fan engagement. Marketing/Media: Brand storytelling, immersive experiences, AR/VR/XR integration, social media engagement, advertising/public relations strategy. Evidence of interdisciplinary teaching or industry practice, bridging communication with applied fields of sports, music, or entertainment marketing. Demonstrated ability to mentor students and connect them with real-world experiential learning opportunities. Experience in online, hybrid, or project-based learning environments. Strong professional network and/or record of industry collaboration."
