      "title": "Student Proctor - College of Law",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-06-09 Department: College of Law Student Svcs College: College of Law Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The College of Law is currently recruiting Student Proctors to join their team. The College has two weeks of exams in the Fall and Spring, and one week in the Summer. Duties to include: Monitor students during test sessions to ensure a secure testing environment. Distribution and collection of examinations. Starting and ending examinations at the appointed times. Report suspected irregularities/unusual behavior to the Registrar. Check in examinations in numerical order as they are turned in. Return all examinations to the Registrar in numerical order at the end of each exam. Minimum Qualifications Requires prior completion of FIU Service Excellence training or completion within first 30 days. Ability to work in a team setting. Basic level of Microsoft Word. Ability to take direction and work independently as needed. Possess solid judgment and decision-making abilities. Possess excellent customer service and communication skills. Ability to work with a large number of people and manage multiple tasks. Ability to work in a multi-ethnic/multicultural environment. Ability to work a flexible schedule including evening and weekend assignments. Job Category Student Assistant Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must end. Work Schedule Hours will vary and may coincide with midterm and final exam periods. Exams scheduled M-Th can start as early as 8:30AM and end as late as 11PM. Exams scheduled on Fridays can start as early as 8:30AM and end as late as 5PM. Advertised Salary $15.00/hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF forma