      "title": "Ultrasound Technician (Per-Diem) - Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2025-11-14 Department: COM Academic Affairs College: Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine Job family: Temporary Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine is currently seeking a Ultrasound Technician (Per-Diem) to join our team of professionals. Duties include: Provides guidance, operation, and instruction to medical students on the principles and techniques of ultrasound imaging using ultrasound technology. Collaborates with faculty members during ultrasound training sessions, helping to demonstrate proper techniques, and troubleshooting technical issues. Assists in the enhancement of ultrasound curriculum, ensuring it aligns with educational objectives and best practices. Maintains and monitors the quality of ultrasound training sessions to ensure students receive a high standard of education. Manages and organizes ultrasound equipment and supplies, ensuring their availability and functionality for training sessions. Maintains accurate records of student performance, training sessions, and equipment maintenance activities. Stays current with advancements in ultrasound technology and teaching methodologies, participating in relevant training and workshops. Operates ultrasound equipment. Supports/assists in simulations to create a virtual healthcare setting. Assists Simulation Specialists and faculty in the use of ultrasound technology for live and simulated teaching activities. Performs other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma or equivalent. ARDMS ® (American Registry for Diagnostic Medical Sonography) certification or equivalent Work Schedule This position is per-diem, the schedule varies. Advertised Salary $34.00 per hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check Temporary Disclosure As a temporary employee, you will not be eligible to participate in all employee benefit programs (e.g., paid leave, retirement, or tuition reimbursement). Under the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (PPACA), a temporary employee who works on average 30 hours or more per week may be eligible to enroll in health care benefits. As a temporary employee, you are also eligible to enroll in supplemental plans (e.g. dental, vision,) which requires full payment on your part. Upon completing an assignment, employees may apply for a position on FIU Careers. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or 