      "title": "Student Office Assistant",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-01-21 Department: Provost and Exec VP Acad Aff College: Provost & Executive Vice President of Academic Affairs Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus Job Category Student Assistant Job Summary The Office of Academic Resource Management is currently seeking Student Office Assistant to join our team of professionals. The Student Assistant in the Office of Office of Academic Resource Management position entails: Greeting visitors and guests who come into the office. Answering phone calls on the main office number. Monitoring the general office email inbox. Filtering and addressing or redirecting questions, concerns, comments, or complaints to the appropriate staff member in the office or university. Providing administrative support to the Office of Academic Resource Management staff which includes printing, copying, faxing, scanning, proof reading and other duties as assigned. Effective logging and tracking of documents that are received by the office or interoffice mail. Maintaining the Academic Affairs upload log updated and assisting with submissions to the PSHR ImageNow system. Preparing coffee, water, and food (if applicable) for meetings. Receiving, sorting, and distributing mail. Signing and receiving packages. Making deliveries and escorting guests across campus when necessary. Providing support for events hosted by the Office of Academic Resource Management. Keeping track of supplies and maintaining the front of the office, kitchen, and the storage rooms. Assist with scanning projects. About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their field