      "title": "Temporary Marketing & Communication Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-08-18 Department: Campaign Planning and Comm College: Advancement Job family: Temporary Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Department of Advancement is currently seeking a Temporary Marketing & Communications Coordinator to join their team of professionals. The Temporary Marketing & Communications Coordinator will work closely with the Director of Marketing in a fast-paced environment to assist with planning, review, and execution of direct communication strategies. Duties include: Oversee the scheduling of communication plans, adjusting timelines and priorities as necessary to ensure smooth execution. Collaborate closely with Alumni partners to ensure all deliverables are met on time. Actively participate in bi-weekly planning and progress meetings on objectives. Partner with the Account Manager and student assistants to ensure updates and changes are implemented. Provide support in asset creation, assisting with content development as needed. Develop, test, and distribute email communication to various stakeholders including Ignite campaigns, Alumni outreach, and Partner engagement. Review and update email distribution lists to ensure accuracy. Assists with writing and content creation for posts, talking points, or website copy. Conducts monthly reviews of email communication and performance, track key metrics and identifying areas for improvement. Update and maintain email performance data (Excel). Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or GED and five (5) years of office or related experience providing administrative support, or coordinating functions of an office or department. Job Category Temporary Temporary Disclosure As a temporary employee, you will not be eligible to participate in all employee benefit programs (e.g., paid leave, retirement, or tuition reimbursement). Under the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (PPACA), a temporary employee who works on average 30 hours or more per week may be eligible to enroll in health care benefits. As a temporary employee, you are also eligible to enroll in supplemental plans (e.g. dental, vision,) which requires full payment on your part. Upon completing an assignment, employees may apply for a position on FIU Careers. Work Schedule 8:30 AM to 5:00 PM Monday-Friday Advertised Salary $15.00-$18.00 per hour. Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cov