      "title": "Student Group Fitness Instructor - Campus Recreation",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-05-21 Department: Wellness & Rec Center MMC College: Division of Student Affairs Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary Campus Recreation is seeking experienced group fitness instructors to join our dynamic fitness team. Candidates must hold a current, nationally accredited group fitness certification and demonstrate a strong passion for motivating and supporting participants in achieving their health and wellness goals. Our group fitness program emphasizes professionalism, evidence-based practices, and a high-energy environment. Responsibilities include leading safe and engaging group fitness classes, creating class formats for different fitness levels, and providing ongoing encouragement and instruction to participants. Duties include: Ability to lead an engaging, and safe group fitness classes for a large student population, including individuals of varying abilities and fitness levels. Proficiency in modifying exercises and adapting programming in real-time to meet. participants' needs while supporting a safe environment. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Clear and effective verbal communication skills to deliver instruction, motivation, and feedback in a group setting. Commitment to maintaining a consistent teaching schedule and communicating in advance regarding absences or coverage needs. Dependable and punctual Instructors are expected to arrive at least 15 minutes prior to the scheduled start of each class to allow adequate time for preparation and setup. Adhere to all university and Campus Recreation policies, procedures, and professional conduct standards. Physical ability to demonstrate exercises, stand for extended periods, and safely lift and move equipment (minimum of 45 lbs overhead). Dedication to ongoing professional development and maintenance of a current, nationally recognized group fitness certification (e.g., ACE, AFAA, NASM, ACSM). Enthusiasm for contributing to a positive, student-centered fitness culture focused on wellness, inclusion, and personal growth. Minimum Qualifications Valid nationally accredited (NCCA-approved) group fitness certification, or license in the format of instruction CPR/ AED/ First Aid certification within 30 days of hire Job Category Student Assistant Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must end. Work Schedule Work flexible hours, including nights and weekends, based on client and facility needs. Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. Disclosures Clery Notice In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act , the University Police department at 