      "title": "Student Specialized Instructor - Campus Recreation",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-05-21 Department: Wellness & Rec Center MMC College: Division of Student Affairs Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary Student/Temporary Specialized Instructor (Martial Arts, Dance, Weight Training, Self-Defense, Wellness) Campus Recreation is seeking enthusiastic and skilled Specialized Instructors to join our dynamic team. We are particularly interested in individuals with expertise in martial arts, dance, weight training, and wellness-focused disciplines such as meditation, sleep health, yoga, and mind-body practices. Candidates must possess a current, nationally recognized certification, appropriate belt ranking, relevant degree in their area of specialization, and/or applicable fitness certification or licensure related to the format of instruction. Our specialized programs emphasize professionalism, evidence-based practices, and a high-energy learning environment. Responsibilities include leading safe and engaging classes, developing class formats appropriate for varying skill levels, and providing ongoing instruction, encouragement, and support to participants. Duties includes: Ability to lead welcoming, engaging and safe specialized small group training sessions for 4-12 participants of varying abilities and fitness levels. Proficiency in modifying activities and adapting programming in real-time to meet participants' needs while supporting a safe environment. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Clear and effective verbal communication skills to deliver instruction, motivation, and feedback in a group setting. Commitment to maintaining a consistent teaching schedule and communicating in advance regarding absences or coverage needs. Dependable and punctual. Instructors are expected to arrive at least 15 minutes prior to the scheduled start of each session and stay for at least 10 minutes following the end of the session to allow: adequate time for preparation, set up, tear down, and engagement with participants. Adhere to all university and Campus Recreation policies, procedures, and professional standards of conduct. Physical ability to demonstrate exercises, stand for extended periods, and safely lift and move equipment (minimum of 45 lbs overhead). Enthusiasm for contributing to a positive, student-centered fitness culture focused on wellness, belonging, and personal growth. Minimum Qualifications Must possess a current, nationally recognized certification, appropriate belt ranking, relevant degree in the area of specialization, and/or applicable fitness certification or license relevant to the format of instruction. Prior teaching or instructional experience in martial arts, self-defense, fitness, or related movement-based disciplines. Current CPR/ AED/ First Aid certification (or obtain within 30 days of hire Job Category Student Assistant Work Schedule Work flexible hours, including nights and weekends, based on client and facility needs Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. Disclosures Clery Notice In c