      "title": "Temporary Development Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-09-16 Department: Development College: Advancement Job family: Temporary Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Development Department is currently seeking a Temporary Development Coordinator to join their team of professionals. Duties include: Office Operations: assists with day-to-day office operations, special projects, internal coordination, stakeholder communications, funding-opportunity review, and the development of corporate and foundation proposals and applications. Working under designated leadership, the coordinator will support evolving departmental priorities, institutional initiatives, and time-sensitive assignments across both functional areas. Team Support & Coordination: Provide essential administrative and operational support to the development team, helping streamline processes, and ensure smooth day-to-day operations so developers can focus on core technical work. Strategic Talent Sourcing: Utilize LinkedIn Sales Navigator and other professional platforms to proactively identify. research, and engage top tier development talent, building a robust pipeline of qualified candidates for current and future technical roles. Recruitment Partnership: Collaborate closely with hiring managers and HR to understand technical requirements, screen initial candidates, and coordinate the interview process from initial outreach through final hiring decisions. Relationship Building: Develop and maintain relationships with potential candidates, technical communities, and recruitment networks to establish FIU as an employer of choice in the competitive development talent market. Data-Driven Recruitment: Track sourcing metrics, candidate pipeline health, and recruitment effectiveness to continuously optimize talent acquisition strategies and report on hiring progress to leadership. Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma or GED and 2 years of experience; OR an equivalent combination of relevant education and/or experience. Job Category Temporary Temporary Disclosure As a temporary employee, you will not be eligible to participate in all employee benefit programs (e.g., paid leave, retirement, or tuition reimbursement). Under the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (PPACA), a temporary employee who works on average 30 hours or more per week may be eligible to enroll in health care benefits. As a temporary employee, you are also eligible to enroll in supplemental plans (e.g. dental, vision,) which requires full payment on your part. Upon completing an assignment, employees may apply for a position on FIU Careers. Work Schedule Monday-Friday 9:00 AM to 5:00 PM Advertised Salary $17.00 per hour. Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to trac