      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer in Economics, Politics, & Philosophy - Adam Smith Center for Economic Freedom",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-06-03 Department: Adam Smith Ctr Eco Freedom College: Provost & Executive Vice President of Academic Affairs Job family: Adjunct Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Information The Adam Smith Center for Economic Freedom is conducting a search for adjunct professorships in economics, politics and philosophy, broadly defined. Adjunct Professors will prepare and deliver relevant instruction using a variety of teaching methods to undergraduate and/or graduate students obtaining a Bachelor of Science or Master of Science in Business and Government Leadership. Instruction will be primarily face-to-face, with occasional online pedagogy. The Adam Smith Center for Economic Freedom Working at the intersection of government policy, management, and the free market, the Adam Smith Center for Economic Freedom is an independent and non-partisan think tank that aims to inspire current and future leaders to develop innovative and effective policies to advance economic freedom and human prosperity. The Center promotes respect, responsibility, excellence and truth-while informed and enlivened by Adam Smith's principles of free market societies and individual freedom. https://freedom.fiu.edu Please note that this pool is open for the 2025-2026 academic year and is reviewed based on departmental needs. Screening of applications will occur as positions become available and continue until positions are filled. Qualified candidates are encouraged to apply to Job Opening ID 537351 at careers.fiu.edu and attach their CV. This pool will remain open until October 31st, 2026. Please submit your (1) brief cover letter addressing why the Adam Smith Center is a particularly strong match for your professional and academic background, (2) professional resume/cv, (3) contact information for at least two references. Letters of reference and transcripts will be requested from finalists at a later date. Please address any questions to freedom@fiu.edu . Applicants are encouraged to review Florida International University's immigration and visa requirements, if applicable, prior to applying: https://hr.fiu.edu/employees-affiliates/working-at-fiu/immigration-process Job Category Adjunct How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have 