      "title": "Educational Program Coordinator (NeighborhoodHELP) - Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-08-19 Department: COM Clinical Affairs College: Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine is currently seeking an Educational Program Coordinator to join our team of professionals Duties: Manages the onboarding, assignment, and training of all undergraduate and graduate level learners to the Neighborhood Help (NHELP) program including but not limited to medical, nursing, social work, Physician Assistant (PA), Graduate Medical Education (GME), and other student learners. Responsible for collecting and distributing required administrative documentation associated with educational placements. Support a team-based household model integrating multiple disciplines and working with academic faculty to Ensure alignment between student learning objectives and household needs. Continuously assess and refine the model based on feedback and outcomes. Identify opportunities to expand interdisciplinary participation and manage partnerships with FIU colleges and academic programs. Additionally. managing the quarterly interprofessional education faculty team meetings. Collaborates with the NeighborhoodHELP evaluator, Office of Medical Education, Academic Faculty to monitor and report on key performance indicators and student learning outcomes. Identify opportunities to improve efficiency, effectiveness, and impact of student involvement. Responsible for ordering, preparing, and distributing medical supply bags for residents and providing other medical supplies, as needed, to learners. Collaborate with program leadership to align student activities with service delivery, including integration of students into mobile units, home visits, and brick-and-mortar services. Performs related duties as required or as directed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree and 1 year of experience; OR 5 years of office or related experience; OR an equivalent combination of relevant education and/or experience. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $40,000 - $42,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Expanded Background Check How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application pr