      "title": "Student Maker Space Proctor",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-07-07 Department: Engineering Deans Office College: College of Engineering and Computing Job family: Student Location: Engineering Center About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The College of Engineering Deans Office currently seeking Student Maker Space Proctor to join their team of professionals. Duties to include: Nestled within the heart of our FIU CEC campus, Maker Space is a beacon of creativity and ingenuity. We are seeking enthusiastic engineering students to join our team as Makerspace Facilitators. As a facilitator, you will play a pivotal role in fostering an environment where innovation thrives. Your responsibilities will include ensuring adherence to safety protocols, monitoring room reservations, and assisting students with the use of air media, tools, and technical equipment. You will also facilitate student project workshops, providing guidance and support as they bring their ideas to life. You will work as a mediator between faculty and students to ensure any use of this space adheres to safety guidelines and all materials and inventory used are approved and allowed including but not limited to appropriate technical equipment, chemicals, safety tools etc. Responsibilities: - Enforce and educate students on Maker Space safety protocols. - Monitor and manage room reservations to ensure fair and organized usage. - Assist students in operating various tools and equipment, including 3D printers, air media, metalworking tools, and other technical devices. - Facilitate workshops and provide hands-on support for student projects. - Maintain and organize the workspace to ensure a conducive environment for creativity and collaboration. - Troubleshoot technical issues and perform routine maintenance on equipment. - Foster a welcoming and inclusive atmosphere, encouraging students to explore and innovate. Minimum Qualifications Requires prior completion of FIU Service Excellence training or completion within first 30 days. Currently enrolled at FIU engineering or computing program. - Strong understanding of safety protocols and best practices in a workshop setting. - Proficiency in using general technical equipment and tools commonly found in a makerspace. - Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. - Passion for creativity, innovation, and hands-on projects. - Ability to work collaboratively and supportively within student and faculty environment. Join us at Maker Space and help empower your peers to turn their visions into reality. Apply today to become a part of our dynamic and inspiring team! Job Category Student Assistant Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must end. Work Schedule Standard 20 hours Advertised Salary $15.00/hour to $20.00/hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. Disclosures Clery Notice In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act , the University Police department at Florida International University provides information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three (3) calendar years. The FIU Annual Security report is available online at: https://police.fiu.edu/download/annual-security-fire-safety-report/ . To obtain a paper copy of the report, please visit the FIU Police Department located at 885 SW 109th Avenue, Miami, FL, 33199 (PG5 Market Station). Pay Transparency Florida International University will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against empl