    "https://pslinks.fiu.edu/psc/jobs/CUSTOMER/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST&Action=U&JobOpeningId=537560&postingseq=1&SiteId=1000&REL_ACTION=Yes": {
      "title": "2026-2027 FIU at I-75, Student Operations Associate",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-07-09 Department: FIU at I-75 College: Vice Provost BBC & Global Job family: Federal Work Study Location: FIU at I-75 Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Advertised Salary $16.00/hour Desired Qualifications Must be an undergraduate or graduate student recipient of Federal Work Study. Ability to communicate effectively and tactfully, both verbally and in-writing. Possess a high sense of responsibility. Ability to provide excellent customer service. Knowledge of PC operations preferred (Windows/Microsoft Office). Ability to work in a multicultural environment. Ability to take direction and work independently. Ability to maintain pleasant working relationships and work well in a team environment. Works well with others and creates a positive team work environment. Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary The FIU at I-75 department, located at the FIU at I-75 campus,'has an opportunity for a student to join their team of professionals. The duties include: Greets, directs, and assists patrons of FIU at I-75, provides general faculty and student support services, and resolves general facility/technical issues as they arise. Serves as a support services contact person at the FIU at I-75 academic center. Assists in coordinating the maintenance and repairs of an assigned building/department. Interprets daily space scheduling reports to monitor room usage, secure room doors, and determine appropriate room configurations. Provides basic technological support to faculty, staff, and students with computing, duplicating, and A/V equipment. Assists with study rooms daily operations including the use of the LibCal software to manage student bookings, provide access to spaces, secure spaces post reservation, and document any study room policy violations. Assists with the daily setup and breakdown of onsite events. Assists with the execution of emergency management procedures during times of emergency. Maintains logs as needed. Understands the admissions application process and necessary documentation that needs to be submitted to complete the admissions application. Reviews documents students are submitting to ensure successful completion of forms and additional documentation. Assist students with uploading of related documents. Escalates problem cases to department's Enrollment Generalist II. Understands and abides by FERPA & HIPPA regulations. Provides general admissions information and assistance to all prospects, inquires, students, etc. Has a clear understanding of the different ways a student can take classes at FIU. This includes non-degree, transient and dual enrollment inquiries. Communicates the university policies and procedures. Must be able to lift up to 30 pounds. Candidate is required to attend a mandatory orientation and training session with the immediate supervisor. Performs other related duties as assigned or as directed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". In order to be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position, be in good performance standing, and have been continuously employed at the University for at least six months. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". In order to be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position, be in good performance standing, and have been continuously employed at 