ds of department. Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Desired Qualifications Must be familiar with Microsoft office Ability to operate mobile inspection devices Must be able to lift up to 30 lbs Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary Environmental Health and Safety is currently seeking a student to join their team of professionals. Duties to include: Conducting monthly inspections of fire extinguishers and annual inspections of fire doors located throughout FIU campuses under the direction of the EH&S Fire Prevention Office. Supporting fire safety training as needed and complete tasks as assigned by the supervisor. This position will require working in office and field settings."
