velopment team, including data entry, database management, and filing. · Assisting with the coordination of volunteer efforts and outreach to alumni and other stakeholders. Other miscellaneous duties as needed To be successful in this role, the ideal candidate should possess strong organizational and communication skills, reverence for confidentiality, attention to detail, and the ability to work independently as well as part of a team. Additionally, experience with fundraising or event planning is preferred (but not required). Job Category Federal Work Study Desired Qualifications Two years experience providing clerical support Intermediate experience with Microsoft Office Suite Research and data collection skills Ability to apply judgment and see projects through to completion Ability to communicate effectively Ability to maintain confidentiality Knowledge of PC operations and software Ability to maintain pleasant working relationships and work well in a team environment Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Work Schedule Hours will vary based on class schedule and needs of the department. Advertised Salary $15.00/Hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. Student Background Checks Background check and fingerprinting is required if the job includes any of the following: Duties: Yes or No Working directly with and/or residing with minors and/or vulnerable persons. No Working in K - 12 schools. (May require DCF Clearinghouse clearance at a cost) No Handling/managing cash, checks, cash transactions, gift card