      "title": "2026-2027 Development, Student Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-07-10 Department: Development College: Advancement Job family: Federal Work Study Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Foundation Development Office is hiring a Student Assistant that will provide administrative support for the staff members in order to be able to fulfill the mission of raising important dollars for our student scholars The Student Assistant will be responsible for the day-to-day administrative operation of the office including but not limited to: Answering phones, taking messages, etc Greeting guests/donors Ordering office supplies (monthly) Assists with paperwork, copying and filing Assist Finance Student Assistant with financials such as gathering and organizing and scanning receipts, preparing expense report backup documents, pay invoices, create requisitions Maintain organization of giveaway materials closet, giveaways and conference room area Support with donor cultivation, solicitation recognition and stewardship efforts- including note writing, gift sending, etc Support donor events, programs, educational pro