tions Must have completed at least one year at FIU (or one semester if Transfer student) Basic event planning and marketing knowledge Honors College membership preferred Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary The Honors College Engagement Student Assistant will support the Engagement Program Manager in the planning, marketing and execution of key Honors College programs and events, including Honors Hours and Honors College Week. Overview of requirements/responsibilities: Reports directly to the Engagement and Program Manager in the Honors College. FWS Students contribute to the direction of the Honors College goals, objectives, and envisionment to ensure they are achieved throughout the year. Assists the Honors College in areas of student programming, event coordination, retention, and assessment initiatives Collaborate with other university departments and offices to implement services/programs that are aimed at increasing the presence of Honors College within the FIU campus and putting emphasis on the Honors College students. Engage in campus-wide outreach to the Honors College student body and general student body through tabling, Honors College Week, Honors Hours, and partnership. Outreach is conducted with student councils, organizations, and residence halls. Propose potential event/programming through either focus group, research, or surveys that are best for the Honors College student body. Alongside creating and research data needed to be shared with the Honors College student body. Perform other related duties as assigned or directed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to this position. Time Breakdown: 30% Working on assigned tasks for Honors College, Assist Program Manager & General Office Support 25% Attend Meetings w./Program Manager, Student Leadership, or Student Interns 15% Tabling/Event Set-Up & Break Down 10% Administrative Tasks with Program Manager 5% Professional 