 in a university sponsored Summer Camp? (Requires DCF Clearinghouse at a cost)? NO Will the position require entering any K-12 schools? (Requires public school system clearance) NO Will the position perform fiscal duties to include budgeting, accounting, or having direct access to cash, checks, gift cards and/or credit/debit cards to include making and/or receiving payments? NO Will the position have control over university-wide operational processes through functional roles or system security access ( Information technology related functions, e.g., Web/Application Developer, IT Technician, Data/Systems Analysts etc.)? NO Will the position drive a university vehicle (including using the golf cart)? (MVR Check only) NO Will the position travel with student athletes to events? NO Is this designated as a position of special trust, responsibility, and sensitive location (Museums, Housing Residential Life, NFSTC, and working with and around minors etc.)? NO Will the position have system access to process payments, print or distribute checks, process corrections, or generate, update, or approve financial transactions that will result in the disbursement of university funds? (Office of Financial Aid, One Stop, or Office of the Registrar (Title IV access) NO Will this position work within the following units that provide health and human services: College of Medicine, College of Nursing, Health Sciences, Physical Therapy, Athletic Training, School of Social Work, Occupational Therapy, Dietetics & Nutrition, Student Health, Psychology, Center for Children & Families? Office of Inspector General (OIG) Checks (Global Watch only) NO Will the position support university sponsored research? (May require Research Extended Background Check) NO Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. Advertised Salary $15.00/Hour Work Schedule Hours will vary based on class schedule and needs of department Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Desired Qualifications Current Florida International University students enrolled during both the Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 semesters and eligible for Federal Work Study. Previous study abroad experience and/or administrative experience preferred. Honors College student is preferred. Must be a self-starter and possess a high level of responsibility and organization. Must have the ability to maintain pleasant working relationships. Must possess effective communication and strong customer service skills. Must be computer literate and knowledgeable in Microsoft Office (specifically Excel and Word), OneDrive, Outlook, Teams, Canva, Mailchimp, and ZOOM. Ability to use graphic tools to create flyers, posts, and info graphics using Adobe Creative Suite & Canva. Should have a reliable method of transportation for work schedules, meetings, and/or events. Should have a laptop, email, and smartphone to work as needed. Ability to work flexible hours as needed. Ability to work on occasional evenings and weekends as needed. Ability to work throughout the Summer 2027 semester to support the Content Creators program. Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary Prospective employees in this role will work with the Honors College Study Abroad area to assist in strategic planning and help execute marketing and communications projects leading up to and throughout the programs Prospective employees must be available in advance for meetings, orientations, and recruitment events. Work closely with Honors College Study Abroad Program Manager to assist in the overall brand and image of Honors Study Abroad Programs marketing. Works closely with Honors College Junior Account Manager to ensure all FIU Branding Guidelines are followed. Collaborate on our social media strategy including analytics and campaign performance tracking. Assist in the creation and development of program-specific HTML coded e-blasts (newsletters). Create engaging text, image, and video content for multiple platforms. Create general and Program-specific social media materials and content. Update website information and content. Maximum of 20 hours per week."
