d at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Desired Qualifications Current Florida International University students enrolled during both the Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 semesters and eligible for Federal Work Study. Previous study abroad experience and/or administrative experience preferred. Honors College student is preferred. Must be a self-starter and possess a high level of responsibility and organization. Must have the ability to maintain pleasant working relationships. Must possess effective communication and strong customer service skills. Must be computer literate and knowledgeable in Microsoft Office (specifically Excel and Word), OneDrive, Outlook, Teams, Canva, Mailchimp, and ZOOM. Should have a reliable method of transportation for work schedules, meetings, and/or events. Should have a laptop, email, and smartphone to work as needed. Ability to work flexible hours as needed. Ability to work on occasional evenings and weekends as needed. Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary Prospective employees in this role will work with the Honors College Study Abroad area to assist with planning and coordination of all program related duties. Prospective employees must be available in advance for meetings, orientations, and recruitment events. Work closely with Honors College Study Abroad Program Manager to assist in the development, recruitment, and logistics of 12 international faculty-led programs. Work closely with the Office of Education Abroad to ensure all deadlines and guidelines are followed. Assist in the recruitment of about 185 Honors College students to participate in Honors Study Abroad programs. This involves recruitment on campus and virtually. Maintain communication with students via email, phone, and class visits. Review and verify student payments and application requirements and communicate deadlines to students. Lead informational sessions for programs. General administrative duties. Maximum of 20 hours per week. Advertised Salary $15.00/Hour"
