      "title": "2026-2027 Office of the Registrar, Student Customer Service Associate",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-07-10 Department: Office of the Registrar College: Enrollment Services Job family: Federal Work Study Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon graduating, FWS employment must end. About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Advertised Salary $15.00/Hour Desired Qualifications Customer service experience. Experience working in higher education. Knowledge of Florida International University policies and procedures. Strong administrative, organizational, and prioritization skills. Familiarity with the use of standard office equipment (e.g. Xerox copier, fax, scanner). Fluency in Microsoft Office, Outlook, Excel, Work and Adobe Acrobat. Experience with CRM or other database software. Experience with PeopleSoft. Flexibility with office hours as needed. Ability to prioritize and multi-task in a fast-paced environment. Works well with others and creates a positive working environment. Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary The Office of Registrars has an opportunity for a federal work-study student to assist staff with day-to-day operations and provide general information. Every employee must behave with the outmost professional judgement while performing the duties assigned. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform these essential functions. Summary: Ability to communicate clearly and concisely with tact and diplomacy in all oral and written communications. Ability to work effectively in a team environment. Ability to exercise appropriate personal initiative and accountability. Ability to handle sensitive information in a confidential manner. Proven ability to execute instructions accurately and in a timely manner. Outstanding interpersonal and active listening skills along with an analytical and critical thinking ability to interpret and respond appropriately to diverse groups of constituents in various situations. Must have exceptional follow-up, follow-through, and attention to details skills, accomplishing tasks with concern for all areas involved. Demonstrates ability to work efficiently and complete tasks in a fast-paced environment amidst interruptions and fluctuating workloads. Customer Service Provide customer service support via telephone, email, and in-person requests. Respond to email from departmental email addresses (transcripts, graduation, and verify). Review documents to ensure accuracy and successful completion of forms and additional documentation. Escalates problems to appropriate SR manager for the functional area. Document records using PantherSoft, ImageNow, Parchment, National Student Clearing House and any other platform used in the Registrar's Office. Support OneStop staff with front counter during peak hours. Student Records Activities Understand and abides by FERPA regulations. Collection and review of sensitive documentation for purposes enrollment verifications, transcript ordering and graduation processing. Review and understand a student's record to problem solve and answer any student questions that may arise. Communicate the university policies and procedures. Provides detailed information to students in accordance with all applicable laws, regulations, and policies, regarding the records. Maintain current knowledge of federal, state, and institutional programs, regulations, policies, and procedures. Processing of enrollment verification requests for past and current terms. Has a clear understanding of the differences in non-degree, transient and dual enrollment students. Transcripts Activities Respond to students, staff, and external constituents regarding transcript inquiries. Interact with third party transcript company for processing of transcript requests and troubleshoot students' transcript issues using third party's company software and portal. Serves as a liaison for the OneStop department to answer transcript related questions. Graduation Activities Process requests for late graduation applications. Process requests for cancellation of graduation applications. Process requests for duplicate diplomas. Assist with graduation functions including commencement fairs and graduation ceremonies. Class Management Activities Process OCM Help Desk tickets from University faculty and staff members. Assist in projects as directed by OCM Assistant Director. Information Technology Activities Assist with running queries. Assist with desktop support. Assist with correction of enrollment reporting. Troubleshooting of hardware and software issues. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". In order to be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position, be in good performance standing, and have been continuously employed at the University for at least six months. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 11:59 pm of the close date. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". In order to be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position, be in good performance standing, and have been continuously employed at the University for at least six months. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 11:59 pm of the close date. Disclosures Clery Notice In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act , the University Police department at