the department. Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Desired Qualifications Ability to work in team settings Communication skills Adaptibilty Interest in wokring with people and learning Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary Job Duties include but are not limited to: Provide support and assistance in the daily work and maintenance of the organization such as Answering phones and emails and directly or indirectly providing assistance. Greeting students as they arrive at the office and determining how best to assist, Taking note during meetings Putting information on social media Helping out with PLTL \"events\" Helping PLTL to fulfill its mission of assisting students with the material in their classes. General clerical and supervisory duties. We are one big team, and everyone helps everyone else out. So, this person would have experience in many facets of the organization and can grow to the degree they are interested in doing so."
