    "https://pslinks.fiu.edu/psc/jobs/CUSTOMER/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST&Action=U&JobOpeningId=537668&postingseq=1&SiteId=1000&REL_ACTION=Yes": {
      "title": "2026-2027 Office of Financial Aid, Student Financial Loans Assistant",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-07-13 Department: Office of Financial Aid College: Enrollment Services Job family: Federal Work Study Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Advertised Salary $17.00/ Hour Desired Qualifications APPLICANT MUST UPLOAD CURRENT FINANCIAL AID ELIGIBILITY EMAIL Knowledge of PC operations and software (Windows). Ability to maintain pleasant working relationships and work well in a team environment. Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary The Assistant to the Financial Aid Loan Coordinator provides leadership and support across the Enrollment Pathway in multi faceted activities associated with Prospects, Admissions, Financial Aid, Registration, Retention, Graduation, etc. These include, but are not limited to, the following: Maintains student records. Drafts correspondence to communicate with students. Analyzes, processes, inputs, maintains, and secure enrollment information into student records. Edits and verifies reports and communications. Provides administrative support for listed Financial Aid programs as needed on a cyclical basis and as directed by supervisor. The Candidate is required to attend a mandatory orientation and training session with the immediate supervisor. Training will prepare the employee for handling specific financial aid inquiries and processing of federal, state, institutional and private aid. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". In order to be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position, be in good performance standing, and have been continuously employed at the University for at least six months. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". In ord