. Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Other information: Ability to work flexible hours as needed Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Current FIU student and eligible for Federal Work Study Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary Florida International University (FIU) (Modesto Maidique Campus) is seeking an individual to serve as a Federal Work Study Training Room Assistant in its Athletics Training Room. The successful candidate will assist the Athletics Department in all facets Athletic Training Room Responsibilities will include but are not limited to: Assists in the coordination and administration of student-athlete (pre-participation/post-season) physical exams Assists with correspondence and securing authorizations for medical referrals for coordination and utilizing the student-athletes primary insurance to assist with cost mitigation' Assists with filing, data entry, scanning, scheduling, and training room organization and cleanliness Assist with hydration Assist with practice and game setup and breakdown Assist with general treatments on student athlete with supervision of Athletic Trainers. Other Information ability to lift heavy equipment, ability to stand or sit for a long period of time, ability to work outside Ability to travel locally & nationally flexible hours nights, weekends, holidays Must be able to stand, walk, jog, and run 'for extended periods during practices, games, and emergency situations. Ability to quickly respond 'to on-field injuries, including running across the field with emergency medical supplies. Frequent bending, kneeling, squatting , and lifting/moving equipment '(up to 50 lbs ), including coolers, training kits, and treatment tables. Work might be performed outdoors in varying weather conditions '(heat, cold, rain), as well as indoors in training rooms and facilities. Must be able to remain alert and physically engaged 'throughout long shifts, including early mornings, evenings, weekends, holidays, and travel with the team as required. Occasional climbing of stairs or stadium seating with equipment may be necessary. Use of hands and arms in repetitive motions 'during taping, bracing, and treatment application. Must maintain high levels of situational awareness and mobility 'in a fast-paced, physically demanding sports environment."
