      "title": "2026-2027 FIU Internship - Library Operations-BBC, Student Library Systems Intern",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-07-14 Department: Library Operations College: Library Operations Job family: Federal Work Study Location: Biscayne Bay Campus Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Advertised Salary $15.00/Hour Desired Qualifications Ability to communicate effectively in both English & Spanish Possess a high sense of responsibility and customer service skills. Ability to maintain pleasant working relationships and work well in a team environment. Must have experience with Windows 7, Windows 10 and MAC OS Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary The Library System Department at BBC Hubert Library has an opportunity for a student to join their team of professionals. This position will assist staff with basic computer troubleshooting, software and hardware installation, and computer maintenance and configuration. Areas of Study: Information Technology, Computer Science, Networking, CybersecurityEssential responsibilities and duties may include, but are not limited to the following: Responsible for desktop support for computer labs areas, staff, laptops, and classrooms. Checks for any problems or issues related to the equipment installed in the classrooms, offices and computer labs. Provides preventive maintenance to equipment (maintains and cleans computer equipment (monitors, CPU's keyboard etc.), VR Headsets, 360 Camera's, Audio Devices) Provides basic software and hardware maintenance, hardware and software installations and upgrades. Cable management, hardware inventory, IT office organization, event setup, etc. This internship opportunity will have an employee supervisor guiding and mentoring student throughout the experience. Student and Supervisor must review learning goals and objectives and participate in a formal meeting at the midpoint and end of the semester to discuss and complete Student Evaluation and Employer Evaluation.By the end of the internship, student will have gained valuable practical experience, learned how to apply theoretical knowledge in practical settings, and experienced real-life challenges and situations. Disclosures Clery Notice In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act , the University Police department at Florida International University provides information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three (3) calendar years. The FIU Annual Security report is available online at: https://police.fiu.edu/download/annual-security-fire-safety-report/ . To obtain a paper copy of the report, please visit the FIU Police Department located at 885 SW 109th Avenue, Miami, FL, 33199 (PG5 Market Station). Pay Transpar