uating, FWS employment must end. Desired Qualifications A willingness to learn and a positive attitude are necessary Ability to safely lift 50 lbs A willingness to do physical work with attention to detail Good communication and organizational skills Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary The Art and Art History Department has an opportunity for a Ceramics Studio Assistant to assist with studio management in Ceramics. The candidate will assist with materials inventory, studio maintenance, basic tool and equipment use, and general oversight of open studio hours. The candidate will complete basic health and safety training provided by supervising Faculty and/or full-time Lab Manager Personal safety equipment will be provided Responsibilities may include maintaining kiln shelves, loading/unloading and firing kilns, mixing clay and glazes, materials inventory, routine studio organizing and clean-up under the direction of the supervising Faculty and/or full-time Lab Manager, as well as general oversight of open studio hours Preference will be given to candidates enrolled in Art and Art History degree programs, but students in other departments with a passion for clay are also welcomed to apply. Disclosures Clery Notice In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act , the University Police department at Florida International University provides information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three (3) calendar years. The FIU Annual Security report is available online at: https://police.fiu.edu/download/annual-security-fire-safety-report/ . To obtain a paper copy of the report, please visit the FIU Police Department located at 885 SW 109th Avenue, Miami, FL, 33199 (PG5 Market Station). Pay Transparency Florida International University will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inqui