esters. Upon graduating, FWS employment must end. Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary The Health Services Administration Department at the Biscayne Bay Campus (BBC) is currently seeking a student to join their team of professionals. The student will perform basic office duties, such as typing, filing, answering phones, data entry, etc. Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check Office of Inspector General (OIG) Checks This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. Student Background Checks Background check and fingerprinting is required if the job includes any of the following: Duties: Yes or No Working directly with and/or residing with minors and/or vulnerable persons. No Working in K - 12 schools. (May require DCF Clearinghouse clearance at a cost) No Handling/managing cash, checks, cash transactions, gift cards, debit/credit cards, and/or cash equivalent. No Information technology (IT) related functions , e.g. Web Developer, IT Technician, etc No Driving on behalf of the university (MVR Check only). No Those working in the Athletics Department who travel with students to events. No Working within museums. No Those working in the Office of Financial Aid, One Stop, or Office of the Registrar (Title IV access). No Special trust, responsibility, and sensitive location. No Working in centers of health and/or counseling care. No Work Schedule Hours will vary based on class schedule and needs of the department."
