      "title": "Student Assistant, Gift Services",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-09-21 Department: Gift Services and Data Process College: Advancement Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary 1- Responsible for scanning documents into the One drive such as originals Gift agreements, pledges, events and more 2- Responsible for sending receipts and pledge reminders 3- Responsible for processing return mail 4- Assisting the full time staff with projects 5- Assisting on ordering supplies for the department 6- Contact units for deposit transmittal and assist creating deposit transmittals for check with no Do assigned to the Foundation following the donor's intent. 7- Responsible for creating GIK (Gift in Kinds), stocks, AT (Athletics) and regular receipts on a daily basics 8- Responsible for the Biographical update queue in Image Now. (All journals are processed in less than 48 hours) 10- Assisting Development officers from different units with updating information in the system 11- Working on special projects to support the division Minimum Qualifications Requires prior completion of FIU Service Excellenc