 and needs of the department Ability to work flexible hours for programmed calendar events in the evenings and/or weekend Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Desired Qualifications Ability to work programs outdoors Tabling/program set up Work a four-hour shift Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary Student Life and Development (SLD) is recruiting Student Alumni Relations Assistant(s) to join their team of professionals This position reports to the Associate Director for Alumni Relations and supports outreach initiatives that foster student engagement across FIU This position will service staff and alumni with a high degree of autonomy in the area of event support, engagement and data entry The role of the SLD Alumni Relations staff is to meet the needs of all alumni guests through the facilitation of programs and data entry and program setups Additionally, this position is responsible for providing customer service/registration for SLD programs, assisting the SLD leadership as needed Duties include: Under direct supervision from the Associate Director, support the planning and execution of events with university partners that focus on engagement opportunities Support management of department social media accounts and departmental marketing initiatives Represent SLD Alumni Relations during tabling events Data entry Other Information Machines and Equipment: Computer, Copy machine Microsoft Office Tabling materials"
