ased on class schedule and needs of the department Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Desired Qualifications Desired Qualifications: 1 year as a Lifeguard at FIU WRC or 2 years lifeguard experience American Red Cross, First Aid, CPR, and AED certifications Lifeguard will maintain certifications within the American Red Cross that pertain to lifeguarding, first aid, CPR, and AED Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary The Wellness and Recreation Center at BBCis currently seeking a Student Lifeguard to join their team of professionals. Duties to include: Oversees lifeguards and manages staff scheduling and coverage of pool hours of operations Assists aquatics coordinator with training and certification of all lifeguard staff Oversees and assist pool operations to include pump room, chemical testing, etc Assists with inventory of pool related supplies and materials Oversees the quality control checks of lifeguard related materials and tools Assist with in service workshops Communicate any operations or personnel issues to appropriate professional staff if necessary Ensures the safety of all participants utilizing the Panther Hall Leisure pool and/or Aquatics Center Monitor and supervise all swimming activities Provides preventive lifeguarding and vigilant observance for informal recreation, rentals, and youth programming Maintains knowledge of current lifeguarding skills in accordance with the American Red Cross and Florida International University Campus Recreation policies and procedures Enforces rules and regulations where applicable Arrives on time for assigned shifts and ensures appropriate supervision of pools Provides a clean and safe leisure pool by performing assigned light cleaning and sanitation duties Provides exceptional customer service and develops and cultivates a positive rapport with patrons Maintains regular communication with the supervisory team and other lifeguards Actively participates in all general and in-service trainings Performs kayaking instruction as assigned Maintains current American Red Cross Lifeguard Certification, First aid, CPR and AED Perform other duties related to the position as assigned"
