th programming. Maintains knowledge of current lifeguarding skills in accordance with the American Red Cross and Florida International University Campus Recreation policies and procedures. Enforces rules and regulations where applicable. Arrives on time for assigned shifts and ensures appropriate supervision of pools. Provides a clean and safe leisure pool by performing assigned light cleaning and sanitation duties. Provides exceptional customer service and develops and cultivates a positive rapport with patrons. Maintains regular communication with the supervisory team and other lifeguards. Actively participates in all general and in-service trainings. Performs kayaking instruction as assigned. Maintains current American Red Cross Lifeguard Certification, First aid, CPR and AED. Perform other duties related to the position as assigned. Desired Qualifications 1 year as a Lifeguard at FIU WRC or 2 years lifeguard experience. American Red Cross, First Aid, CPR, and AED certifications. Lifeguard will maintain certifications within the American Red Cross that pertain to lifeguarding, first aid, CPR, and AED. Job Category Federal Work Study Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Work Schedule Hours will vary based on class schedule and needs of the department. Advertised Salary $18.00/Hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. Student Background Checks Extended Background Check is required if the job includes any of the following responsibilities. Some may also require a Fingerprint Check: Duties: Yes or No Will t