ipts, Python scripts, and other automation scripts as necessary Escalate issues and questions to management as needed Participate in meetings to gain process knowledge and guidance on assigned projects Assist in identifying automation and AI opportunities Contribute to continuous improvement initiatives Lead presentations demonstrating AI technologies and their use cases Validate AI-generated outputs for accuracy and compliance Job Requirements: Passion for growth, professional development, and learning new skills Knowledge or understanding of database query languages such as SQL is a plus but not required Strong problem-solving and critical thinking skills Excellent verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills Strong analytical and quantitative problem-solving abilities Familiarity with data management and visualization tools Job Category Federal Work Study Desired Qualifications College major in mathematics, science, business administration, or a related field preferred Ability to work both independently and collaboratively with others Demonstrated ability to take initiative and drive results Ability to create dashboards and reports Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Work Schedule Schedule based on department needs and class schedule Advertised Salary $15.00/hr Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. Student Background Checks Extended Background Check is required if the job includes any of the following responsibilities. Some may also require a Fingerprint Check: Duties: Yes or No Will the posi