      "title": "2026-2027 - Marketing and Analytics Student Assistant",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-07-16 Department: COB Off of Grad Enroll and Rtn College: College of Business Job family: Federal Work Study Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Office of Graduate Enrollment and Retention at FIU's College of Business is seeking a highly motivated, creative, and responsible Student Marketing and Analytics Assistant This Federal Work Study position supports digital marketing initiatives, content creation, social media engagement, and analytics reporting to enhance graduate program visibility and student engagement Key Responsibilities Content Creation & Digital Marketing Extract shareable quotes and content from alumni, faculty, and student interviews/videos for website and marketing use Research business-related topics and collaborate with content strategists to develop and distribute content across multiple platforms Update program information on external websites and post special events on the FIU Calendar Assist in developing email campaigns, including testing across devices and compiling performance reports Process and analyze survey data to inform marketing strategies Upload prospective student leads from external sources into Salesforce CRM Respond to inquiries across digital platforms and direct prospective students to appropriate recruiters Support the Interaction Designer by sourcing appropriate images and music for videos and advertisements Social Media Management Assist in managing and maintaining the social media content calendar Design engaging visual content (graphics and videos) tailored for social media platforms Capture and edit photos and videos from events to create dynamic content Draft captions and written content for LinkedIn, email campaigns, and other digital channels Monitor and respond to comments, messages, and mentions to foster audience engagement Contribute innovative ideas to support FIU Chapman's social media growth and brand consistency Assist with organizing content and managing digital assets Job Category Federal Work Study Desired Qualifications Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, and computer skills Understanding of search engine optimization (SEO) or digital content creation Ability to work well in a fast-paced, team-driven environment Strong organizational skills Familiarity with content creation, social media platforms, and engagement strategies Interest in social media, marketing, digital media, or communications Basic design or photo/video editing skills preferred (eg, Canva, Adobe, or similar tools) Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Work Schedule Schedule based on department needs and class schedule. Advertised Salary $17.00/per hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Backgro