      "title": "2026-2027 COB Chapman Graduate School, Student Program Associate",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-07-16 Department: COB Chapman Graduate School College: College of Business Job family: Federal Work Study Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The COB Chapman Graduate School department is seeking a student to join their team of professionals The selected candidate will provide leadership and support across the College of Business Chapman Graduate School The selected candidate will provide support to the Global Recruitment and Operations office for the Chapman Graduate School and assist with multi-faceted activities and events as scheduled by the College Job duties include: Provide excellent customer service to all prospects and current students via emails, phone calls, and in-person. Provides administrative support for the office to include telephone coverage, copier projects (including overhead preparation and/or PowerPoint presentations), mail handling, supplies control, and necessary communications internally and externally. Document telephone calls and answer general email inquiries for all international applicants Assist with planning and execution of recruitment events, open houses, and seminars Providing information to prospective students about requirements, deadline dates, and general information Scan and link documents to the student's accounts on ImageNow system Update students' applications in the PantherSoft and CRM systems Initially qualify leads based on academic credentials, professional background and subject area of interest Utilize a collaborative and proactive approach connecting leads with recruiters Utilize various software programs, including MS Office and CRM System and assist with data entry and clerical tasks, as needed Create and answer cases for leads/prospects in CRM System Assist in the pulling of student data for program records and submission of program rankings Creates and maintains study abroad application portals in CRM system Assists in design and development of marketing materials for study abroad programs Oversees follow up for international recruitment event leads and contacts. Serves as initial point of contact for international undecided prospects. Maintains Office of Global Initiatives social media Additional duties as assigned relevant to the position Job Category Federal Work Study Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Work Schedule Hours will vary based on class schedule and needs of the department. Advertised Salary $15.00/Hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. Student Background Checks Background check and fingerprinting is required if the job includes any of the following: Duties: Yes or 