d. Desired Qualifications Desired Qualifications: Ability to work well in a team environment Ability to communicate effectively Possess a high sense of responsibility and customer service skills Ability to take direction and work independently as needed Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary Job Description: The College of Business is currently seeking a student to join their team of professionals The selected candidate will provide support in multi-faceted activities and events for the Department of Global Leadership and Management (GLAM) Duties to include: Assist in the coordination of department functions Provide the front office and administrative staff with support (eg filing, e-mailing, mail duties, phone calls and data entry, scanning and inquiries) Maintain our inventory of office, students and faculty supplies Collect syllabi and office hours for all faculty members in the department at the beginning of the semester Create PDF documents needed for expense reports and credit card reconciliation paperwork Research conference details, such as conference agenda and recommended conference hotels to expedite travel authorization process and expense report process Contact COB AV for audio and visual Performs other related duties as required or as directed the omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position"
