      "title": "2026-2027 COB Finance, Student Program Assistant",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-07-16 Department: COB Finance College: College of Business Job family: Federal Work Study Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Academic Department of Finance in the College of Business is seeking a student to join their team of professionals in the MMC campus. This is an hourly position. The student could work in between semesters (semester breaks) if available. The student will work 20 hours per week, with an average of 4 hours per day, until their FWS financial aid award is depleted, if applicable. Duties: Answer and direct incoming phone calls. Assist students, faculty, and the general public in person. Perform general clerical duties, including filing, copying, scanning, and organizing documents. Sort and distribute incoming mail; prepare outgoing mail and packages. Assist supervisor with travel arrangements for professors and guests as needed. Use various software programs for recordkeeping, scheduling, and communication. Monitor exams to ensure compliance with FIU's testing policies and procedures. Maintain accurate and up-to-date student and departmental records. Perform data entry with a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Assist faculty and students with departmental academic needs. Support professors with basic Canvas and course-related requests. Collaborate with departmental staff to coordinate, organize, and execute special events. Contribute to the preparation of materials for faculty, staff, and students. Communicate with students via email in a professional and timely manner. Run office-related errands as needed. Maintain strict confidentiality regarding student and faculty information. Provide general administrative and office support as assigned. Job Category Federal Work Study Desired Qualifications Punctual Excellent telephone etiquette Advanced knowledge of Microsoft Office Great customer service skills Ability to take directions and work independently Have initiative Maintain confidentiality when dealing with highly sensitive materials and information Bilingual English/Spanish is a plus but not a must Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Work Schedule Hours will vary based on class schedule and needs of the department. Advertised Salary $16.00/Hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. Student Background Checks Background check and fingerprinting is required if the job includes any of the following: Duties: Yes or No Working directly with and/or residing with minors and/or vulnerable persons. No Working in K - 12 schools. (May require DCF Clearinghouse clearance at a cost) No Handling/managing cash, checks, cash transactions, gift cards, debit/credit cards, and/or cash equivalent. No Information technology (IT) related functions , e.g. Web Developer, IT Technician, etc No Driving on behalf of the university (MVR Check only). No Those working in the Athletics Department who travel with students to events. No Working within museums. No Those working in the Office of Financial Aid, One Stop, or Office of the Registrar (Title IV access). No Special trust, responsibility, and sensitive location. No Working in centers of health and/or counseling care. No How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". In order to be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position, be in good performance standing, and have been continuously employed at the University for at least six months. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status 