 enrolled at FIU with a minimum of 6 credit houses in a course of study leading to a degree or a financial aid eligible certificate. Ability to work some nights and weekends. Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary The selected candidate will provide support in multi-faceted activities and events for Graduate Business School Admissions & Financial Aid Teams. Provides administrative support to COB Graduate Admissions & Financial Aid Teams. Provide excellent customer service to all prospect and current students via emails, phone calls, and in-person. Scan and link documents to student's account on image now system Distribute mail to all departments and staff in the Chapman Graduate School. Assist with the preparation of ID's transfers, Travel Authorizations, Cash Advances, Expense Reports and requisitions. Order supplies for the office as needed. Assist with posting of communications to prospects and current students. Assist with financial aid reports as assigned. Assist the Admissions & Financial Aid Team with open house events. Additional duties as assigned relevant to the position. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". In order to be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position, be in good performance standing, and have been continuously employed at the University for at least six months. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am o