      "title": "Student Research Assistant",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-07-17 Department: Center for Children and Fam College: College of Arts, Sciences and Education Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Center for Children and Families is currently seeking a Student Research Coordnator to join their team of professionals. - Coordinates day-to-day activities of the project. Works closely with the Principal Investigator (PI) in the implementation of activities associated with research and projects. - Perform a variety of functions involved in the collection, complication, documentation, analysis of research data and assures the confidentiality of the data - Recruits research participants and administers intake and follow-up assessments - Manages communication with parents and teachers to complete behavioral ratings. - Interprets and implements policies and procedures as they apply to an assigned area - Assists with completion of study reports and treatment recommendations - Responds to quality control queries and attends weekly staff meetings to review ongoing work - May travel to local schools to complete classroom observations and meetings. Minimum Qualifications At least 3 semesters of FIU work experience or related experience outside the University with satisfactory or higher from prior student appointment. Requires a letter of recommendation from one prior supervisor. Requires prior completion of FIU Service Excellence training or completion within first 30 days. Ability to work in a team setting. Advanced proficiency of Microsoft Office Suites. Ability to take direction and work independently as needed. Ability to maintain confidentiality when dealing with highly sensitive information. Knowledge of PC operations and specialized software programs, such as PantherSoft and Salesforce. Ability to communicate clearly and concisely, verbally, and in writing. Possess a high sense of responsibility and customer service skills. Ability to solve problems independently. Organizational and time-management skills. Job Category Student Assistant Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must end. Work Schedule Monday - Friday 8:30PM- 5:00PM Available to wrok flexible schedule Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check Fingerprint Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. Advertised Salary $15.00 - $22.00 an hour How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this accoun