      "title": "2026-2027 FIU Arboretum Assistant",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-07-23 Department: Biology College: College of Arts, Sciences and Education Job family: Federal Work Study Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Biology is currently seeking a student to join their team of professionals. Overall, help develop the FIU Arboretum, a diverse collection and outdoor classroom of trees, shrubs, lianas (and some non-woody plants) from around the world 1) Help create educational materials for the FIU Arboretum These duties include: make and deploy temporary labels for plants with their scientific and common names and their native range, and help order and deploy permanent labels if funding is obtained Digitize student-written stories for the Palmetum palms and make the stories accessible to the public through a barcode on the tree's label 2) Survey labeled trees and shrubs on campus These duties include: explore outdoors and find all labeled trees on campus, create a database of the labeled trees and their locations, and match the data collected to a campus tree map This information will help us to increase the accreditation level of the Arboretum 3) Source trees and shrubs needed to complete the recent plantings for the Research exhibit of the Arboretum in the OE courtyard and IoE, and possibly for the Medicinal trees exhibit upon approval These duties include: search for sources of the trees (preferably local nurseries), contact vendors to determine tree availability, and keep a spreadsheet of the vendors, tree sizes, and prices 4) Perform other related duties as needed You will work in close collaboration with Arboretum Interns and Volunteers and the Office of University Sustainability Job Category Federal Work Study Desired Qualifications 1) Ability to use and accurately enter data into online spreadsheets 2) Ability to perform online searches for botanical information, and discern reliable sources 3) Ability to learn to use a simple labeling machine and neatly paste the labeling tape onto plastic signs 4) Basic computer and internet skills and proficiency with programs such as Word and Excel Ability to learn new programs or apps as needed 5) Ability to explore outdoors on campus and keep accurate records of findings Ability to use GPS is a plus 6) Ability to conduct basic business email correspondence and phone conversations 7) Ability to follow directions, work independently and also collaborate with others 8) Interest in botanical garden development or urban environmental education Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Work Schedule Hours will vary based on class schedule and departmental needs. Advertised Salary $15.00/hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. Student Background Checks Extended Background Check is required if the job includes any of the following responsibilities. Some may also require a Fingerprint Check: Duties: Yes or No Will the position provide unsupervised direct care, treatment, education, training, instruction, supervision, or recreation to vulnerable populations such as minors, the elderly, or those with disabilities? ( Expanded + Fingerprint Check required) N Will this role be in the Center for Children and Families (CCF) or the Childrens' Creative Learning Center (CCLC)? N Will this role be part of a university-sponsored summer camp or afterschool program? ( Those providing services in Camps will require DCF Clearance at a cost) N Will this role require entering any K-12 schools? ( Those providing services in K-12 Schools will require MDCPS/BCPS Clearance at a cost.) N Will this role have direct access to cash, checks, gift cards, credit cards, debit cards, or make and receive payments? N Will this role conduct IT related functions, e.g. IT Technician, Data Analyst, Application Developer, etc.? N Will this role require driving of a university-owned motor vehicle (including golf cart and other utility vehicles)? N Will this role travel with Athletics teams to events? N Will the role be in a special trust/sensitive location? N Will this role be in the Office of the Registrar, Office of Financial Aid, or One Stop? N Will this position work within the following units that provide health and human services: College of Medicine, College of Nursing, Health Sciences, Physical Therapy, Athletic Training, School of Social Work, Occupational Therapy, Dietetics & Nutrition, Student Health, Psychology, Center for Children & Families? Office of Inspector General (OIG) Checks (Global Watch only) N Will this role perform or support research? (Mark No if this is a Graduate Assistant contract (GA, RA, TA)) N How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have no