      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-07-28 Department: Career and Talent Development College: Innovative Education and Student Success Job family: Federal Work Study Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Career and Talent Development Department is currently seeking a Student Peer Coach to join their team of professionals Duties to include performing resume, cover letter, and CV critiques online and in person during designated Drop-In program Providing basic career advice to students and alumni Maintains accurate data records Supports office staff Interacts and collaborates with staff working on projects in a team environment Primary Responsibilities: -Perform resume, cover letter, and CV critiques online and in person during designated Drop In program -Collect walk-in student and alumni numbers for data purposes weekly -Assist resources committee in making and updating office PowerPoint workshops such as Resume Writing, Salary Negotiation, and Career Readiness etc -Provide basic career advice to students and alumni -Educate students on the Career & Talent Development Department services and encourage students to be active -Create and modify student and alumni accounts on Handshake platform -Assist Career Development & Management team in creating workshop calendars as needed -Assist in office programs such as Career Fairs, Commencement Fair and other career related events -Perform other office duties as assigned by supervisor Benefits of Becoming a Student Peer Coach: -Professional Development of Self -Develop Career Readiness skills such as: Communication, Work Ethic, Teamwork, Public Speaking, Event Planning, Problem Solving, etc -Support peers with professional development -Build and grow connections with Student Organizations -Getting more involved within your college experience -Great Resume Builder! Job Category Federal Work Study Desired Qualifications Other Related Skills: -Leadership experience -Strong presentation, public speaking, communication, and interpersonal skills -Exceptional time management and reliability -Takes initiative and follows through on necessary details -Willingness to work in a team setting and build rapport with other On Campus Recruitment staff members -Demonstrates professional communication when working with supervisors and students -Overall interest in assisting FIU students with career and job search topic -Be knowledgeable in marketing with social media Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Work Schedule Schedule based on department needs and class schedule. Advertised Salary $15.00/per hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. Student 