      "title": "Student Guest Services Assistant - Wolfe University Center",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-07-30 Department: Wolfe University Center College: Division of Student Affairs Job family: Student Location: Biscayne Bay Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Student Centers at the Wqolfe University Center (WUC) on the Biscayne Bay Capmus (BBC) are currently seeking a Student Guest Services Assistant to join their team of professionals. Duties will include providing assistance at the Computer Lab, Game Room and Welcome Center/Information Desk. Responsibilities amongst all areas will include providing coverage to other units as needed, completing all required student trainings, and representing the Division in University events such as Commencement. Computer Lab Provide excellent customer service to all students, faculty/staff and external guests. Enforcing Computer Lab policies and procedures Checks in and patrons wanting to Computer Lab. Assists guests with printing, photocopying and scanning of materials. Oversees all events being hosted in the lab such as e-sports tournaments and orientation sessions. Maintain and upkeep the appearance of the Computer Lab. Provides good customer service to all patrons. Make recommendations for service enhancements at the Computer Lab. Provides assistance if any of the systems are presenting an issue Refills supplies as needed. Report faulty equipment in need of repair. Be cross-trained with Welcome Center and Game Room policies and procedures. Game Room Provide excellent customer service to all students, faculty/staff and external guests. Enforcing Game Room policies and procedures. Assist guest with RecRe rentals. Make recommendations for service enhancements at the Game Room. Assist with surveying Game Room patrons. Assist with the upkeep of the Game Room space. Report faulty equipment in need of repair. Be cross-trained with Welcome Center and Computer Lab policies and procedures. Welcome Center/Information Desk Provide excellent customer service to all students, faculty/staff and external guests. Answer general inquiries about the University Direct guests to specific locations on campus Record and tracks lost and found items into Reclaim Hub system Maintain organization of lost and found items Report things they observe on the main floor, as needed Be cross-trained with Computer Lab and Game Room policies and procedures. Minimum Qualifications Customer service knowledge Ability to take direction and work independently as needed. Ability to maintain confidentiality when dealing with highly sensitive information. Job Category Student Assistant Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must end. Work Schedule Weekdays and Weekends. Up to 20 hours per week. Advertised Salary $15.00/hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. 