graduating, FWS employment must end. Job Category Federal Work Study Job Summary The CPHSW School of Social Work is currently seeking a student to join their team of professionals. Duties to include: Provide excellent customer service to all students, faculty, staff, and visitors in person, by telephone, and via email Provide support to office staff and faculty in a collaborative team environment Demonstrate a willingness to assist with a wide range of office and departmental needs Follow instructions and complete tasks as directed by supervisors, faculty, and staff Maintain flexibility in carrying out assigned duties and responding to changing priorities Maintain a professional, dependable, and punctual work ethic Complete tasks accurately and in a timely manner Maintain confidentiality and professionalism when handling office materials, records, and interactions Answer and direct telephone calls Greet and assist visitors to the School Assist faculty and staff with student appointments and scheduling needs Create flyers, informational materials, and other communications Distribute daily mail to faculty and staff mailboxes Perform scanning, data entry, filing, copying, and document management tasks Assist with event setup, breakdown, and logistical supportTake minutes and maintain records for meetings as assigned Perform opening and closing office procedures Run errands within the building and across the University campus as needed Provide administrative support to the Director, Associate Director, and PhD Program Director Assist with scheduling meetings, appointments, and academic program activities Prepare, organize, and distribute materials for meetings, events, presentations, and departmental initiatives Maintain accurate records, databases, and tracking systems related to departmental activities and student programs Support departmental communications, including announcements, reminders, and informational outreach to students, faculty, and staff Assist with the administrative coordination of student e-portfolios, including communication, scheduling, submission tracking, and record maintenance Support capstone project activities by coordinating schedules, maintaining documentation, communicating with students and faculty, and assisting with presentation logistics Assist with planning and administering departmental colloquia, seminars, research presentations, and related academic events Coordinate logistics for student academic programming, including room reservations, attendance tracking, preparation of materials, and event support Assist with collecting, organizing, and maintaining assessment materials, evaluations, and program-related documentation Support student engagement and academic success initiatives through effective administrative coordination and communication Perform special projects and additional duties as assigned that are relevant to departmental operations and student programming"
