ls to assess participant learning. Conducts performance assessments and provides constructive feedback to enhance course quality and learning outcomes. Trains on locating, identifying, and safeguarding potential sources of digital evidence. Teaches on how to search for digital media, while documenting and preserving data in accordance with accepted standards Instructs on report preparation, and verbal and written reporting of digital media examinations. Teaches the use of computer forensic hardware. Trains on media exploitation and recovery of digital evidence in accordance with U.S. federal and state laws. Minimum Qualifications Positions under National Forensic Science Technology Center will require Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and 5 years of experience in related field; OR nine (9) years of relevant training and/or military experience; OR an equivalent combination of relevant education, training, and/or military experience. Desired Qualifications Experience in intelligence analysis, document and media exploitation, and/or digital forensics. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $88,621 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Working Condition(s) Required to spend 50% or more of time operating a computer. Work requires some physical effort in the handling of materials, boxes or equipment. May occasionally be required to work outdoors. Pre-Employment Requirements Clearance by the Department of Defense Drug Screening Fingerprinting Check Expanded Background Check Other Information This position is funded by an external funding source (e.g. a grant or contract). Ability to work flexible hours as needed. May be required to work on University holidays. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication re