      "title": "SOBEWFF® Student Office Assistant, Biscayne Bay Campus",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-08-19 Department: South Beach Wine and Food Fest College: Business and Finance Job family: Student Location: Biscayne Bay Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary SOBEWFF® Student Program Office Positions Multiple Part-Time Openings | 2026'2027 Festival Season The South Beach Wine & Food Festival® Experiential Learning & Community Engagement Program is seeking creative, organized, resourceful, and dependable FIU students to join the SOBEWFF® Student Program office team for the 2026'2027 Festival cycle. These paid, part-time positions support the recruitment, onboarding, communication, administration, systems, marketing, and Festival-week operations that make it possible for more than 1,500 FIU student and community participants to take part in SOBEWFF® each year. Applicants may be considered for one or more of the positions below based on their interests, experience, skills, availability, and the needs of the program. All roles combine office-based responsibilities with hands-on support during peak recruitment periods and Festival week. Position Details: Primary work location: SOBEWFF® Student Program Office, Chaplin School of Hospitality & Tourism Management, 3000 NE 151st Street, HM 243, North Miami, FL 33181 Additional locations: FIU campuses, recruitment locations, Festival event locations, and Student Program HQ in Miami Beach, depending on the position and assignment Festival availability: Full availability is required February 22'March 1, 2027, including early mornings, late evenings, weekends, and extended operational shifts as needed Schedule: Up to 20 hours per week. Positions are primarily in person; remote work is not available Pay: $16.00 per hour Available Positions: Marketing, Graphic Design & Social Media Assistant This role helps generate excitement about the SOBEWFF® Student Program by creating recruitment content and supporting graphic design, email marketing, social media, and other digital communications. During Festival week, the focus shifts to capturing the student experience across multiple events and coordinating a small team of student content creators. Create recruitment graphics, flyers, email campaigns, presentations, and social media content using existing brand resources and templates. Support the Student Program's content calendar, social media channels, Mailchimp campaigns, and participant communications. Capture, collect, edit, and organize photography and video content for real-time Festival coverage and future recruitment campaigns. Maintain organized marketing assets and ensure materials follow SOBEWFF® and FIU brand standards. Recruitment & Event Programming Assistant This role directly supports the Recruitment Program Manager with recruitment outreach, participant onboarding, event programming, and community engagement. The position combines detailed administrative work with recruitment events and hands-on Festival support. Coordinate recruitment tablings, presentations, class visits, and outreach activities across FIU and partner locations. Maintain recruitment calendars, Airtable systems, contact lists, outreach trackers, and event reservations. Assist with applicant screening, interview scheduling, and onboarding for student and community participants through Connecteam. Prepare recruitment materials, signage, giveaways, and tabling kits and help track related inventory. Respond to participant questions, troubleshoot routine onboarding issues, and support recruitment and Festival operations. Recruitment & Event Operations Coordinator Recruitment Coordinators play a central role in recruiting, onboarding, communicating with, and supporting the more than 1,300 FIU student and community participants involved in the Festival. This position combines participant support and detailed administrative work with staffing coordination, recruitment outreach, and hands-on Festival operations. Assist with the recruitment, onboarding, placement, and ongoing support of Festival participants. Guide students through Connecteam onboarding, including profile completion, required forms and waivers, participation requirements, and shift selection. Maintain consistent communication with assigned student and community participants and respond to questions through email, phone, and approved communication platforms. Support on- and off-campus recruitment initiatives, including tabling events, presentations, and outreach activities. Assist during Festival week with participant check-in, staffing support, scheduling, meal distribution, and operational troubleshooting, followed by attendance tracking and scholarship-processing support after the Festival. Systems & Operations Assistant This role supports the systems, technology, scheduling workflows, and operational tools used by the Student Program. During Festival week, Student Program HQ becomes the Assistant's primary responsibility. This is not an event-assigned role; the Assistant helps keep the program's home base organized and operational. Support Connecteam, Setmore, Airtable, Mailchimp, interview scheduling, staffing assignments, and participant onboarding systems. Help troubleshoot routine issues involving printers, laptops, Wi-Fi, phones, accounts, and other program equipment. Maintain process documentation, training resources, operational trackers, and system workflows. Help set up, operate, and break down Student Program HQ and maintain equipment, supplies, printing, and participant-support systems. Monitor real-time staffing updates, receive and organize deliveries, and escalate issues when leadership attention is required. Program Operations & Administration Assistant This is a broad, high-trust role that serves as the primary assistant to the Senior Program Manager and supports day-to-day administration and operations across the Student Program. The position is ideal for someone who can manage competing priorities, protect sensitive information, anticipate needs, and keep projects moving without constant direction. Support recruitment, hiring, onboarding, staffing, training, participant communication, and office administration. Maintain calendars, records, trackers, project files, meeting materials, and operational documents. Coordinate across Program Managers, Assistants, Coordinators, students, and other Festival staff. Research answers, resolve routine issues independently, and escalate matters that require manager approval. Assist with Festival logistics, Student Program HQ operations, reporting, and special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Must be a current FIU student enrolled during both the Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 semesters. Able to work consistently in person and maintain the required weekly schedule. Full availability during Festival week, February 22'March 1, 2027. Strong written and verbal communication, organization, time management, and follow-through. Professional, dependable, adaptable, responsive, and comfortable working in a fast-paced environment. Able to manage multiple responsibilities, use available resources, solve routine problems independently, and recognize when an issue should be escalated. Comfortable learning and using technology platforms such as Connecteam, Airtable, Mailchimp, Canva, Figma, Setmore, Microsoft Office, Outlook, Zoom, and Google Workspace, as applicable to the assigned role. Able to attend assignments at FIU campuses, recruitment locations, Student Program HQ, and Festival event locations as required. Willing to assist with light physical and event-related tasks, including moving supplies, materials, equipment, or participant items when needed. Preferred Experience Previous SOBEWFF® participation, Coordinator experience, or event experience. Leadership, customer service, hospitality, recruitment, marketing, communications, administration, logistics, or campus-involvement experience. Experience managing calendars, spreadsheets, databases, content, digital systems, or operational workflows. Photography, videography, graphic design, social media, or content-creation experience for applicants interested in the Marketing role. Bilingual communication skills are a plus. What You Will Gain These positions provide hands-on experience supporting one of the nation's largest food and wine festivals. Students will build transferable skills in communication, leadership, project coordination, recruitment, marketing, technology, logistics, problem-solving, and large-scale event operations while working alongside Festival Leadership, FIU departments, community partners, and hospitality industry professionals. Minimum Qualifications At least 3 semesters of FIU work experience or related experience outside the University with satisfactory or higher from prior student appointment. Requires a letter of recommendation from one prior supervisor. Requires prior completion of FIU Service Excellence training or completion within first 30 days. Ability to work in a team setting. Advanced proficiency of Microsoft Office Suites. Ability to take direction and work independently as needed. Ability to maintain confidentiality when dealing with highly sensitive information. Knowledge of PC operations and specialized software programs, such as PantherSoft and Salesforce. Ability to communicate clearly and concisely, verbally, and in writing. Possess a high sense of responsibility and customer service skills. Ability to solve problems independently. Organizational and time-management skills. Desired Qualifications Job Category Student Assistant Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must end. Work Schedule Hours will vary based on class schedule and departmental needs. Advertised Salary 15$-25$ Pre-Employment Requirements Student Background Checks Extended Background Check is required if the job includes any of the following responsibilities. Some may also require a Fingerprint Check: Duties: Yes or No Will the position provide unsupervised direct care, treatment, education, training, instruction, supervision, or recreation to vulnerable populations such as minors, the elderly, or those with disabilities? (Fingerprint Check required) Will this role be in the Center for Children and Families (CCF) or the Childrens' Creative Learning Center (CCLC)? Will this role be part of a university-sponsored summer camp or afterschool program? ( Those providing services in Camps will require DCF Clearance at a cost) Will this role require entering any K-12 schools? ( Those providing services in K-12 Schools will require MDCPS/BCPS Clearance at a cost.) Will this role have direct access to cash, checks, gift cards, credit cards, debit cards, or make and receive payments? Will this role conduct IT related functions, e.g. IT Technician, Data Analyst, Application Developer, etc.? Will this role require driving of a university-owned motor vehicle (including golf cart and other utility vehicles)? Will this role travel with Athletics teams to events? Will the role be in a special trust/sensitive location? Will this role be in the Office of the Registrar, Office of Financial Aid, or One Stop? Will this position work within the following units that provide health and human services: College of Medicine, College of Nursing, Health Sciences, Physical Therapy, Athletic Training, School of Social Work, Occupational Therapy, Dietetics & Nutrition, Student Health, Psychology, Center for Children & Families? Office of Inspector General (OIG) Checks (Global Watch only) Will this role perform or support research? (Mark No if this is a Graduate Assistant contract (GA, RA, TA)) Other Information Working Condition(s) How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. Disclosures Clery Notice In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act , the University Police department at Florida International University provides information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three (3) calendar years. The FIU Annual Security report is available online at: https://police.fiu.edu/download/annual-security-fire-safety-report/ . To obtain a paper copy of the report, please visit the FIU Police Department located at 885 SW 109th Avenue, Miami, FL, 33199 (PG5 Market Station). Pay Transparency Florida International University will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or (c) consistent with the contractor's legal duty to furnish information. Notice of Non-Discrimination FIU is a State University System of Florida member, Equal Opportunity, Equal Access, and Affirmative Action Employer for individuals with disabilities and veterans. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment decisions, programs, and events without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, or protected veteran status. For inquiries regarding non-discrimination, contact FIU's Office of Civil Rights at 305.348.2785 or email ocr@fiu.edu. Reasonable Accommodation Statement Should you need an ADA accommodation to participate in a University event, program, or activity or need to request materials in an accessible format, please contact FIU's Office of Civil Rights (OCR) at 305-348-2785 or accommodations@fiu.edu. All requests for ADA accommodation or accessible materials for this event must be submitted to OCR at least seven (7) business days prior to the event or at the earliest possible opportunity."
    },
