      "title": "Coordinator of Administrative Services - Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-08-28 Department: COM Academic Affairs College: Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine is currently seeking a Coordinator of Administrative Services to join our team of professionals Duties: Coordinates administrative support in the Office of Medical Education by assisting with tasks across multiple committees. Collects and tracks alumni teaching participation data for program evaluation Assists in recruiting, onboarding and training of Alumni for teaching related activities. Assists in creating and distributing annual alumni survey and analyzing data, including teaching interests and mentorship availability. Assists with preparing annual program outcome reports for Alumni Teaching and Academic Advising, including pulling and organizing referrals, satisfaction, and completion data to support CQI and LCME documentation. Develops on-boarding processes and materials for new advisors/coaches in collaboration with the leadership team. Organizes events/meetings for advisors including scheduling, agenda, setup and break down Assists with mapping data entry and maintaining advisor roster and any necessary assignment changes. Schedules advising and /coaching appointments for students, along with follow ups and documentation of these appointments. Tracks meetings with students to ensure that all students have annual meetings, and that all faculty time is properly recorded. Develops and maintains records for students excused absences, rescheduling and professionalism concerns. Organizes, tracks, completes and maintains advising/coaching files. Coordinates with the Office of Student Affairs (OSA) for the purpose of proper student record keeping and appropriate exchange of information. Liaises with the HWCOM Information Technology team on the design, planning, implementation, and troubleshooting of technology used to manage advising processes, including Student Folio. Performs essential duties in emergencies (e.g., hurricanes, storms) and/or any other university emergency closing. Is expected to report to work as needed during university emergency closing, given appropriate notification from Department administrator. Performs related duties as required or as directed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two (2) years of office or related experience providing administrative support, or coordinating functions of an office or department; OR six (6) years of office or related experience; OR an equivalent combination of relevant education and/or experience. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $40,000-$42,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. Disclosures Clery Notice In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act , the University Police department at Florida International University provides i