      "title": "2026-2027 Graduate FWS Office of Scholarships",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-09-01 Department: Office of Scholarship College: Enrollment Services Job family: Federal Work Study Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Office of Scholarships is currently seeking a Graduate Federal Work Study (GFWS) student to support scholarship operations, financial wellness initiatives, emergency aid operations and student success efforts This position is intended for a graduate student who can apply advanced communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills to assist with scholarship administration, financial wellness programming, and student outreach while providing exceptional customer service: Duties to include: Assist with scholarship administration, including processing awards, revisions, cancellations, and Departmental Scholarship Authorization Forms Review student records for accuracy, resolve Salesforce cases, perform data entry, and assist with resolving discrepancies in student records Draft professional correspondence related to scholarship eligibility, awards, and student inquiries Assist with scholarship-related operational projects and office initiatives Support Financial Wellness programming by assisting with workshops, presentations, outreach events, and educational materials Assist with financial wellness coaching operations, appointment scheduling, and student resource distribution Help coordinate financial wellness events and promote available resources to students Provide exceptional customer service to prospective and current students via phone, email, virtual, and in-person appointments Assist students with general questions related to scholarships, financial wellness resources, emergency aid, and referring them to appropriate campus partners when needed Represent the Office of Scholarships & Financial Wellness at orientations, recruitment events, and campus presentations by communicating scholarship opportunities, financial wellness resources, deadlines, and university processes Maintain confidentiality of student records and perform general administrative and special project duties as assigned Job Category Federal Work Study Who May Apply Students enrolled at FIU, who have been awarded Federal Work Study (FWS) as part of their Financial Aid Award package. Student must be enrolled with a minimum of six (6) credit hours in a course of study leading to a degree or a Financial Aid eligible certificate, during Fall, Spring, and Summer semesters. Upon credits decreasing, award being canceled, or graduating, FWS employment must end. Work Schedule Hours will vary based on class schedule and departmental needs. Advertised Salary $15.00/hr Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. Student Background Checks Extended Background Check is required if the job includes any of the following responsibilities. Some may also require a Fingerprint Check: Duties: Yes or No Will the position provide unsupervised direct care, treatment, education, training, instruction, supervision, or recr