      "title": "Senior Project Manager (Buffalo New York)",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-06 Department: Center for Children and Fam College: College of Arts, Sciences and Education Job family: Administrative Location: Off-Campus National About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary Coordinates the subject recruitment and study assessment visits alongside of the PIs. Collects phone screens and intake materials and provide them to study psychologists for eligibility review. Screens all collected data for missing items. Supervise other full time and temporary staff. Manages project scope, schedule, cost, quality, risks, human resources, communications, and procurement. Assists in the development of study manuscripts and reports Works closely with the Principal Investigator to coordinate all aspects of the research project pertaining to recruitment, compliance with project timeline and progress, compliance with FIU regulations, and outreach activities. Manages project scope, schedule, cost, quality, risks, human resources, communications, and procurement. Works closely with the PI in developing guidelines for the research studies Manages and tracks the distribution of qiftcard of project's participants. Serves as an University card user for departmental transactions. Adheres to University credit card policies and procedures. Supervises project staff and monitor project staff performance. Assistant with clinical evaluations and oversight of data collection and management. Works closely with the Pl in developing guidelines for the research studies Ensures that staff is aware of grant protocols and is in accordance with grant timeline. Trains staff and volunteers Supervises staff and delegates staff effort appropriately across projects to ensure all project goals are met and staff effort is appropriately delegated. Serves as an University card user for departmental transactions. Adheres to University credit card policies and procedures. Develop REDCap data management systems for each project. Assist the principal investigator with IRB proposals, completion of annual reports, and ensure all staff complete required trainings. Assist in the hiring, training, and retention of staff. Serve as a member of the search committee for all new hires. Ensure adequate equipment, supplies, and maintenance of materials is in place in the facility. Assists in the development of study manuscripts and reports Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in a related field with four (4) years of project and/or management experience. Desired Qualifications Experience working with children and families as well as prior research experience. Experience working in a community mental health setting with project management experience. Proficiency with database management Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $55,000 - $65,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Fingerprinting Check Expanded Background Check Other Information This position is located in Buffalo New York This position is funded by a contract, grant, or external partnership Ability to work flexible hours as needed. Ability to travel locally How To A