      "title": "Student Facility Operations Assistant - Campus Recreation MMC",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-09-09 Department: Wellness & Rec Center MMC College: Division of Student Affairs Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Wellness & Recreation Services (WRC)-Campus Recreation department is currently seeking a Student Facility Operations Assistant to join their team of professionals. Duties include: Always provide premiere customer service. Responsible for the cleanliness and upkeep of locker rooms, training rooms, floors, mats, windows, doors, ledges, garbage bins of all indoor and outdoor areas/fields/courts. Assist Building Supervisor in reporting and documentation of all injuries, incidents, or damaged equipment. Complete regular daily detailing of all fitness equipment and continuously re-racking weights. Responsible for communicating policy violations to all patrons not in compliance in the WRC. Assist supervisors with room/event setups and breakdowns. Knowledgeable of cleaning supplies uses and equipment to perform the work assignments. Knowledgeable of WRC and University policies and procedures for emergency management. Communicate effectively and professionally through two-way radio with all co-workers and supervisors. Responsible for turning in all lost and found items to the appropriate lost & found location Assist with enforcing evacuation procedures in the event of any fire alarms and/or emergencies. Maintain constant communications with supervisor and respective administrators. Must be able to lift up to 50 lbs. Other duties may be assigned by supervisors. Communicate any operations or personnel issues to appropriate professional staff if necessary. Job Category Student Assistant Advertised Salary $15.00/hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and a