      "title": "Temporary Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-09-16 Department: Community Engagement College: College of Arts, Sciences and Education Job family: Temporary Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Program Coordinator provides administrative and accounting support to the Senior Program Coordinator and helps to ensure the organization's day-to-day financial records and processes are accurate, organized, and up to date. This position assists with accounts payable, financial recordkeeping, documentation, and other routine finance-related responsibilities as needed as well as donor data and development support. Key Responsibilities Assist the FIU ASAS Senior Program Coordinator with day-to-day accounting and financial administrative tasks. Process and track invoices, payments, reimbursements, and other expenses. Assist with accounts payable Enter and maintain accurate financial information in the organization's accounting system. Organize and maintain financial records, receipts, invoices, contracts, and supporting documentation. Help track payments, outstanding balances, deposits, and other financial transactions. Assist with tracking grant and program expenses to ensure costs are properly documented Maintain confidentiality of financial, employee, donor, and organizational information. Assist the Senior Program Coordinator with other financial and administrative duties as assigned. Other tasks may include sending out staff Meeting Agenda for the bi-weekly calls, answering phone calls, and helping Program Director (s) with operational tasks for FIU ASAS Programs. Assist with event planning/coordination and execution. Donor Data and Development Support Manage and maintain the organization's donor CRM/database, ensuring accurate and up-to-date donor records, gifts, and contact information. Process donor acknowledgments, including weekly thank-you letters (often system-generated), annual/end-of-year giving letters, and other donor correspondence. Prepare donor, fundraising, and contribution reports as needed and assist with maintaining accurate records for reconciliation with Finance. Provide administrative and logistical support to the Director of Development and Marketing for fundraising events, campaigns, donor communications, and other development activities & tasks. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree; OR four (4) years of office or related experience; OR an equivalent combination of relevant education and/or experience. Positions under National Forensic Science Technology Center will require Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization in related field; OR an equivalent combination of relevant training and/or military experience. Job Category Temporary Temporary Disclosure As a temporary employee, you will not be eligible to participate in all employee benefit programs (e.g., paid leave, retirement, or tuition reimbursement). Under the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (PPACA), a temporary employee who works on average 30 hours or more per week may be eligible to enroll in health care benefits. As a temporary employee, you are also eligible to enroll in supplemental plans (e.g. dental, vision,) which requires full payment on your part. Upon completing an assignment, employees may apply for a position on FIU Careers. Work Schedule 10:00am - 4:00pm 20 - 30 Hours August - May Advertised Salary $20 - $23 per hour Pre-Employment Requirements How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curricul