      "title": "Media Exploitation Trainer DOMEX/CELLEX (Fort Bragg, NC)",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-09-17 Department: Nat'l Forensic Science Techno College: Division of Research Job family: Administrative Location: Off-Campus National About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary Provides training mission activities by delivering digital media exploitation (DOMEX) and cellular phone exploitation (CELLEX) instruction in a manner that ensures effective understanding and application of skills taught. Develops, reviews, and refines lesson plans in accordance with the program. Evaluates and assesses student baseline understanding of tasks. Delivers instruction in classroom and scenario settings. Performs ongoing evaluation of student knowledge and skills and provides verbal feedback as well as written evaluations. Reviews, refines, updates if necessary, and comment on lesson plans. Writes personal lesson outlines in support of existing Programs of Instruction and lesson plans. Designs and develops training materials in support of lesson plans, POI guidelines. Develops realistic training scenarios to replicate real-world operations. Plans, develops, and implements training courses in support of POI. Develops and implements evaluation tools to assess participant learning. Conducts performance assessments and provides constructive feedback to enhance course quality and learning outcomes. Develops and implements evaluation tools, and performs assessment of participation learning. Trains on locating, identifying, and safeguarding potential sources of digital evidence. Teaches on how to search for digital media, while documenting and preserving data in accordance with accepted standards. Instructs on report preparation, and verbal and written reporting of digital media examinations. Explains/teaches using computer forensic hardware. Trains on media exploitation and recovery of digital evidence in accordance with U.S. federal and state laws. Teaches on the exploitation of Global Positioning Systems (GPS) capabilities, satellite, Code Division Multiple Access (CDMA) and Global System for Mobiles (GSM) technologies. Trains on the exploitation of foreign cellphone technologies. Trains on the exploitation of automobile telematics, and unmanned systems platforms (UXS). Minimum Qualifications Positions under National Forensic Science Technology Center will require Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and 5 years of experience in related field; OR nine (9) years of relevant training and/or military experience; OR an equivalent combination of relevant education, training, and/or military experience. Desired Qualifications Digital Media Exploitation/Computer Forensics and Cellular Phone Exploitation subject matter expert. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $88,621 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Working Condition(s) Required to spend 50% or more of time operating a computer Work requires some physical effort in the handling of materials, boxes or equipment. May occasionally be required to work outdoors. Pre-Employment Requirements Clearance by the Department of Defense Drug Screening Fingerprinting Check Expan