      "title": "Graduate Student Tutor",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-09-17 Department: Center for Academic Success College: Innovative Education and Student Success Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Center for Academic Success is currently seeking a Graduate Student Tutor to join our team of student support professionals. Duties to include: Provide individual and/or group tutoring to undergraduate students in assigned courses and subject areas. Assist students in developing effective study strategies, problem-solving skills, and a deeper understanding of course material. Support students with course-related questions while encouraging independent learning and critical thinking. Maintain accurate records of tutoring sessions, student attendance, and required reports through the department's tutoring system. Communicate student concerns, course-related needs, and recurring academic challenges to the appropriate professional staff. Assist with developing and implementing academic support activities, workshops, and other departmental programs as needed. Participate in tutor training, staff meetings, and professional development opportunities. Assist with maintaining a welcoming and supportive learning environment for students. Follow departmental policies, procedures, and guidelines related to tutoring and student support services. Provide feedback to professional staff regarding tutoring needs, resources, and opportunities to improve student services. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Desired Qualifications Job Category Student Assistant Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must end. Work Schedule Advertised Salary $15/hour to $25/hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. Other Information Working Condition(s) How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. 