ndently Organizational and time management skills Job Summary The Wolfsonian is hiring a paid Exhibitions + Curatorial Intern for spring 2027. The Exhibitions and Curatorial Intern at The Wolfsonian will play a role in supporting various aspects of exhibition development, with an emphasis on curatorial work. This internship offers training in the museum profession, an overview of museum exhibition operations, and an introduction to the work curators do to develop an exhibition. Tasks include updating exhibition checklists, conducting research to support exhibition development, preparing materials from past exhibitions for the museum's website, and supporting other functions related to curatorial and exhibition work. The Exhibitions and Curatorial Intern will: Gain an understanding of museum exhibition development. Engage in the inner workings of museum operations. Have access to Wolfsonian student enrichment activities such as career roundtables, a resume/cover letter writing workshop, and beyond. This internship is held in person at 1001 Washington Ave, Miami Beach 33139. The Wolfsonian is an art and design research center in South Beach with a collection of more than 200,000 items from the modern age (1850 to 1950). Required Materials Resume, cover letter, and writing sample (500 words max) Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. Advertised Salary $19.00 per hour Work Schedule This internship lasts 12 weeks during the spring semester, from January to April. The internship requires a commitment of 180 hours over the course of the 12 weeks of the internship period (15 hours per week). Weekly schedules are flexible but must coincide with the regular office hours of the Curatorial staff (Monday through Friday, 9am to 5pm), and hours must be spread evenly across the duration of the internship. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. Student Background Checks Extended Background Check is required if the job includes any of the following responsibilities. Some may also require a Fingerprint Check: Duties: Yes or No Will the position provide unsupervised direct care, treatment, education, training, instruction, supervision, or recreation to vulnerable populations such as minors, the elderly, or those with disabilities? (Fingerprint Check required) Will this role be in the Center for Children and Families (CCF) or the Childrens' Creative Learning Center (CCLC)? Will this role be part of a university-sponsored summer camp or afterschool program? ( Those providing services in Camps will require DCF Clearance at a cost) Will this role require entering any K-12 schools? ( Those providing services in K-12 Schools will require MDCPS/BCPS Clearance at a cost.) Will this role have direct access to cash, checks, gift cards, credit cards, debit cards, or make and receive payments? Will this role conduct IT related functions, e.g. IT Technician, Data Analyst, Application Developer, etc.? Will this role require driving of a university-owned motor vehicle (including golf cart and other utility vehicles)? Will this role travel with Athletics teams to events? Will the role be in a special trust/sensitive location? Will this role be in the Office of the Registrar, Office of Financial Aid, or One Stop? Will this position work within the following units that provide health and human services: College of Medicine, College of Nursing, Health Sciences, Physical Therapy, Athletic Training, School of Social Work, Occupational Therapy, Dietetics & Nutrition, Student Health, Psychology, Center for Children & Families? Office of Inspector General (OIG) Checks (Global Watch only) Will this role perform or support research? (Mark No if this is a Graduate Assistant contract (GA, RA, TA)) How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. Disclosures Clery Notice In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act , the University Police department at Florida International University provides information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement,