      "title": "Student Digital Content Systems Intern with The Wolfsonian",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-09-18 Department: The Wolfsonian College: The Wolfsonian Job family: Student Location: The Wolfsonian About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must end. Job Category Student Assistant Desired Qualifications Experience working with photography, video, graphic design, multimedia, or other digital content Familiarity with Adobe Creative Cloud applications such as Adobe Premiere Pro, Photoshop, or Bridge Interest in digital asset management, information systems, metadata, archives, museums, libraries, or cultural heritage collections Familiarity with file organization, metadata, naming conventions, shared storage systems, databases, or digital workflows Interest in learning how technology can improve access to and management of digital information Minimum Qualifications Interest in digital media, technology, information systems, museums, communications, or related fields Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Comfort working with digital files, folders, and shared storage systems Ability to learn and apply consistent file management and documentation practices Ability to work in a team setting Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite Ability to take direction and work independently as needed Ability to maintain confidentiality when dealing with sensitive information Comfort working across PC and Mac environments Ability to communicate clearly and concisely, verbally and in writing Possess a high sense of responsibility Ability to solve problems independently Organizational and time management skills Job Summary The Wolfsonian is hiring a paid Digital Content Systems Intern for spring 2027. The Digital Content Systems Intern at The Wolfsonian will support the Content + Interpretation department in improving how the museum organizes, manages, and accesses its growing digital media collection. Working across photography, video, graphics, exhibition media, metadata, and shared digital resources, the intern will gain experience with the systems and workflows that support digital content throughout a museum. The internship will focus on assessing and organizing existing digital assets, identifying opportunities to improve access and efficiency, and helping develop practical systems for file management, naming conventions, metadata, storage, and retrieval. The intern will also help consolidate existing multimedia into shared digital resources and may help identify and prepare assets for use across the website, social media, exhibitions, press, public programs, and other communications. Through this work, the intern will gain experience at the intersection of digital media, information organization, technology, and museum practice. The Digital Content Systems Intern will: Gain experience with digital content systems and digital asset management in a museum environment. Help inventory, organize, and document existing museum photography, video, graphics, and multimedia. Assist in developing consistent file-naming conventions, folder structures, metadata, and digital media workflows. Help consolidate existing multimedia into shared digital resources that are easier for museum staff to access and use. Learn how digital assets are stored, tracked, retrieved, and distributed across different museum projects and platforms. Assist with identifying and preparing digital media for websites, social media, exhibitions, press, public programs, and other communications. Gain an understanding of how digital content moves through different stages of creation, storage, management, and public use. Have access to Wolfsonian student enrichment activities such as career roundtables, a resume/cover letter writing workshop, and beyond. This internship is held in person at 1001 Washington Ave, Miami Beach 33139. The Wolfsonian is an art and design research center in South Beach with a collection of more than 200,000 items from the modern age (1850 to 1950). Required Materials Resume and Cover Letter Work Schedule This internship lasts 12 weeks during the spring semester, from January to April. The internship requires a commitment of 180 hours over the course of the 12 weeks of the internship period (15 hours per week). Weekly schedules are flexible but must coincide with the regular office hours of the Content + Interpretation staff (Monday through Friday, 9am to 5pm), and hours must be spread evenly across the duration of the internship. Advertised Salary $19.00 per hour Student Background Checks Extended Background Check is required if the job includes any of the following responsibilities. Some may also require a Fingerprint Check: Duties: Yes or No Will the position provide unsupervised direct care, treatment, education, training, instruction, supervision, or recreation to vulnerable populations such as minors, the elderly, or those with disabilities? (Fingerprint Check required) Will this role be in the Center for Children and Families (CCF) or the Childrens' Creative Learning Center (CCLC)? Will this role be part of a university-sponsored summer camp or afterschool program? ( Those providing services in Camps will require DCF Clearance at a cost) Will this role require entering any K-12 schools? ( Those providing services in K-12 Schools will require MDCPS/BCPS Clearance at a cost.) Will this role have direct access to cash, checks, gift cards, credit cards, debit cards, or make and receive payments? Will this role conduct IT related functions, e.g. IT Technician, Data Analyst, Application Developer, etc.? Will this role require driving of a university-owned motor vehicle (including golf cart and other utility vehicles)? Will this role travel with Athletics teams to events? Will the role be in a special trust/sensitive location? Will this role be in the Office of the Registrar, Office of Financial Aid, or One Stop? Will this position work within the following units that provide health and human services: College of Medicine, College of Nursing, Health Sciences, Physical Therapy, Athletic Training, School of Social Work, Occupational Therapy, Dietetics & Nutrition, Student Health, Psychology, Center for Children & Families? Office of Inspector General (OIG) Checks (Global Watch only) Will this role perform or support research? (Mark No if this is a Graduate Assistant contract (GA, RA, TA)) Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be