      "title": "Parking and Transport Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-09-21 Department: Parking and Transportation College: Operations and Safety Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Parking Manager will be responsible for managing the day-to-day operations and administration for department operations. Audits current procedures to monitor and improve efficiency of operations. Manages, supports and provides direction to Parking & Transportation team members and assists in the development of program policies, procedures, assessments and evaluations. Ensures the control process of data systems are met. Monitors and measures service metrics and utilizes data to develop standards, improvements and changes to process. Provides guidance and support to front line team members. Assists with procedure development and ensures adherence in operations. Ensures that customer satisfaction is maximized by maintaining the highest level of service thresholds and initiatives that are aligned with the FIU Parking and Transportation Services standard. Manages and coordinates operational staffing needs for projects and assignments. .Serves as a liaison between the various departments of FIU to support the department's initiatives Plans and directs operations improve productivity and efficiency and ensure staff coverage. Trains, supervises, and evaluates parking staff to ensure high performance and adherence to service standards. Conducts periodic evaluations to assess system functionality and customer satisfaction. Collaborates with university leadership on strategic initiatives to enhance transportation and parking services. Performs essential duties in any emergencies such as hurricanes, public health emergencies, and/or any other university emergency closing. The employee is expected to be available to report to work as needed during university emergency closing with appropriate notification of a department administrator. Performs other related duties as required or as directed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Oversees on-demand, shuttles and golf cart transportation services, coordinate with technology vendors and service providers to enhance user experience and system integration. Manages and optimizes parking management software for permitting and enforcement, analyzing system data to identify trends, enhance operational efficiency, and implement necessary improvements. Works with IT and vendors to resolve system issues, implement upgrades, and maintain cybersecurity protocols. Trains staff in software functionalities and best practices. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four (4) years of related experience; OR eight (8) years of related experience; OR an equivalent combination of relevant education and/or experience. Desired Qualifications Maintenance operations experience Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $50,000 - $55,000 Work Schedule End time: 2:30 PM End time: 11:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check Driver's License Check Other Information Ability to work flexible hours as needed. Ability to work occasional evenings, weekends and at locations outside of the University Travel to FIU Campus Ability to work occasional evenings, weekends, and holidays. Ability to Travel to FIU Locations and/or FIU Campuses. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached docume