      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-09-21 Department: Office of Admissions College: Enrollment Services Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Office of Admissions is currently seeking an energetic, hardworking and professional student to serve as a student recruitment specialist at FIU. Students will get opportunities for professional development activities, become well informed on university departments, get to be part of our selective team and have the opportunity to show their FIU spirit by giving tours of our campus to hundreds of prospective students throughout the year. Responsibilities will include: Conduct tours of MMC to prospective students and select university partners and stakeholders. Staff the Office of Admissions welcome desk to answer questions and provide information to prospective students. Input contact card information into FIU database for prospective students. Manage and create content for the Join FIU social media accounts. Create welcome packets with FIU collateral pieces for prospective student groups, FIU departments, and Office of Admissions recruiters. Maintain and update an inventory list of materials and supplies maintained for admissions-related events. Support supervisors with annual Admissions events, including but not limited to Fall Showcase and Admitted Student Day at MMC and BBC. Remains up to date on FIU policies and practices in order to accurately inform prospective students about details related to the University. Receive and maintain all trainings/licenses related to specific Admissions/Enrollment functions (examples include but are not limited to working the reception area, instant messaging with students via Live Chat, and others). Performs other related duties as required or as directed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications Customer service knowledge Basic level of Microsoft Word. Ability to take direction and work independently as needed. Ability to maintain confidentiality when dealing with highly sensitive information. Desired Qualifications Desired qualifications Customer service knowledge. Proficiency with Microsoft Office programs Ability to take direction and work independently as needed. Consistent attendance and punctuality is required. Ability to maintain confidentiality when dealing with highly sensitive information. Experience working in a customer service environment. Experience with university admissions process. Experience managing and creating social media content for professional accounts. Job Category Student Assistant Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must 