      "title": "Financial Analyst 2 - Hebert Wertheim College of Medicine",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-06 Department: COM Finance and Administration College: Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine is currently seeking a Financial Analyst II to join our team of professionals. Duties include: Assists with design of financial forecasting spreadsheets, budget preparation, and variance reports for OAA and its associated programs. Supports the Assistant Director with organizing budget packages and related analyses. Tracks and reconciles the quarterly clinical teaching services payments for OAA and its Academic Programs. Reviews, logs, and approves financial purchases made through the FIN360 sharepoint site or University Card Solutions. Assists with overseeing the live instructional worksheet process including hosting/creating training workshops, monitoring end user completion, and updating end user with live instructional worksheet updates. Requests, collects, and organizes quarterly the per click report for the various Period 3 and Period 4 sites for the Office of Medical Education. Assists in processing and gathering proper approvals for new clinical operating agreements and renewals. Responds inquiries from vendors, University departments, students and/or other constituents and assists with problem resolution. Assists HWCOM's Operating and the Financial Planning team during peak budget season inputting data onto the Panthersoft system. Assists the OAA and its academic programs with financial aspects of special projects. Hosts financial systems trainings (e.g., FIN360, honorarium/contract processing) upon request from program stakeholders (e.g., coordinators, program managers, or directors). Performs budgetary transactions for the College of Medicine, including the generation of Smart Bills, Journals IDs and budget amendments. Performs related duties as required or as directed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in related discipline and two (2) years of experience in related field or Master's degree in related discipline. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $57,000 - $62,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Expanded Background Check How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resum