      "title": "Financial Aid Officer III (One Stop)",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-09-29 Department: One Stop College: Enrollment Services Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary Serves as the Financial Aid Liaison and primary escalation point for the Onestop Office resolving complex financial aid issues. Interprets Title IV regulations, provides high level counseling to students and families with questions regarding financial aid and enrollment service inquiries through timely customer services via telephone, emails, and in-person. Trains university staff on financial aid policies and procedures. Analyzes applicants and their family's personal circumstances to establish their ability to contribute toward the cost of education. Counsels current and prospective students on application procedures, eligibility criteria, program requirements, and other financial aid concerns. Delivers timely customer service to constituents and support units. Provides customer service support via telephone, email, in-person, and via live chat to execute efficient, expedient, and quality solutions. Assists Financial Aid Office with complex program processing when not resolving Onestop escalated cases. Contributes to the development and delivery of strategic departmental goals and objectives. Assists with recruitment. Facilitates university orientation and high school outreach to present financial aid information to prospective students and parents. Interprets and effectively communicates federal, state, and institutional regulations specific to Title IV funds for administrators, faculty, staff, and students. Develops and delivers comprehensive financial aid training programs for university staff and administrators. Works directly with the Onestop Office to investigate and resolve complex student financial aid issues, overriding systems or applying professional judgment where regulatory exceptions allow. Maintains strict adherence to all federal, state institutional, and NCAA rules and regulations governing financial aid and student eligibility. Performs other duties as assigned. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four (4) years of financial aid or related experience or a Master's degree and two (2) years of financial aid or related experience. Departmental Requirements Must be able to obtain clearance for National Student Loan Data System (NSLDS) access, which requires no default on federal financial aid, within 60 days of employment. Must adhere to federal, state, institutional, and NCAA rules and regulations. Desired Qualifications Advance proficiency with Student Information Systems and federal databases. Proven ability to research and analyze complex problems related to student financial aid administrative rules and policies. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $60,000 - $62,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Expanded Background Check Other Information Ability to work flexible 