      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-09 Department: Office Of The President College: Office of the President Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary Student Assistant ' Office of the President The Student Assistant provides administrative and operational support to the Office of the President. This position is well suited for a dependable, professional, and detail-oriented student who can manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced executive office environment while maintaining discretion and confidentiality. Job Duties Provide general administrative support, including preparing documents, organizing files, scanning, copying, and maintaining office records. Assist with preparation and organization for meetings and events. Welcome visitors and respond to routine telephone, email, and in-person inquiries in a courteous and professional manner. Support special projects, events, and university initiatives coordinated through the Office of the President. Maintain accurate contact lists, mailing lists, spreadsheets, and other office tracking documents. Coordinate deliveries, mail, supplies, and other routine office needs. Handle confidential or sensitive information with discretion and in accordance with university policies. Collaborate professionally with university leadership, faculty, staff, students, trustees, alumni, and external guests. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Requires prior completion of FIU Service Excellence training or completion within first 30 days. Ability to work in a team setting. Intermediate level of Microsoft Word and Excel. Knowledge of PC operations and specialized software. Ability to take direction and work independently as needed. Ability to maintain confidentiality when dealing with highly sensitive information. Job Category Student Assistant Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must end. Work Schedule Preferred schedule: 1:00 - 5:00 PM, Monday - Friday. Advertised Salary $15.00/hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you