      "title": "Junior Voice Communications Engineer",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-12 Department: IT Network Services College: Division of Information Technology Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary This position will assist with the installation, configuration, maintenance, refresh and basic troubleshooting of campus voice communications systems, VoIP infrastructure and related telecommunications hardware and software. Assists with maintaining enterprise voice systems, PBX/VoIP architectures, and user endpoints, extensions and voicemail under the guidance of senior engineers. Responds to routine service tickets, isolates minor network or telephony connectivity issues, and implements standard fixes. Communicates directly with users through phone, email, ticketing systems and MS Teams, including proactive follow-up during troubleshooting. Assists with moves, adds, changes, and deletions (MACD) of telephone extensions, voicemail accounts, and communication features for faculty and staff. Works with other groups within Network Engineering and Telecommunications to support the day-to-day operations of the voice environment. Maintains accurate network diagrams, configuration logs, system configurations, and operational documentation for voice infrastructure up to date. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in a computer related field; OR four (4) years of experience in a computer related field; OR an equivalent combination of relevant education and/or experience. Desired Qualifications Working knowledge of networking fundamentals including TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, routing, switching, VPNs or firewalls. Experience supporting voice technologies such as VoIP, SIP, RTP, PBX, PSTN, DID, or related telecommunications services. Strong troubleshooting, analytical, and critical thinking skills with the ability to independently solve technical issues. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $49,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Driver's License Check Expanded Background Check Other Information Ability to Travel to FIU Locations and/or FIU Campuses. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application includin