      "title": "Coordinator Administrative Services - University Compliance",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-15 Department: University Compliance College: Office of the President Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary Under administrative direction, is responsible for the coordination of the day-to-day operations of the University Compliance Office(s). Makes and implements decisions using independent judgement. Requires knowledge of business administration and office practices and procedures in order to perform moderately complex duties in supporting operations of the University Compliance Office(s). Coordinates and manages special functions and activities. Manages/performs all administrative support functions and provides assistance with all personnel matters. Assists with the coordination of the day-to-day administrative operations of the Office of Compliance. Provides assistance with managing all matters pertaining to personnel which includes updating/creating position descriptions, assisting with the recruitment and on/off boarding process, and maintaining the department's HR files. Provides support in the oversight of Compliance webpages and platforms. Maintains project and administrative filing systems, and all other departmental records as well as the retention of those records. Assists in tracking and coordinating staff's continuing professional education requirements and internal project management systems. Coordinates the schedule and activities of the Office's Student Assistants. Assists on matters directed to the Compliance Office by University and community constituents. Coordinates incoming issues and determines referral and/or response. Serves as point-of-contact on matters directed to the Compliance Office by University and community constituents. Coordinates incoming issues and determines referral and/or response. Serves as a liaison with the University community in setting up meetings, conferences and other functions. Coordinates and assists in the preparation and distribution of all reports and correspondence including: compliance reports, memos, status reports, and annual work plan documents. Assists in writing, editing, marketing, and publishing University Compliance Office communications. Oversees the management of the Compliance Officer's calendar, analyzes appointment requests and determines the most efficient use of his/her time. Provides training/conducts presentations including the University Compliance presentation for the New Employee Experience. Conducts Visual Compliance searches and supports export control issues and inquiries. Assists the University Compliance Officer in coordinating the activities of Work Groups that are brought together to address compliance initiatives on behalf of the University and in disseminating information to the University community regarding initiatives. Provides administrative support to the compliance project teams that includes preparing meeting agenda, presentation, and documenting meeting information. Organizes and supports the administration and tracking of various compliance workflows. Adheres to University rules, regulations, and procedures. Provides administrative support to the department that includes staffing the front desk and greeting guests as needed. Distributes mail and faxes as needed. Answers incoming calls and provides assistance and information to callers. Assists in managing the compliance email accounts. Provides other office support as needed. Performs other related duties as assigned or as directed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Coordinates the department's travel arrangements and prepares travel authorizations and expense reports reimbursements as needed. If needed, ensures travel purchases are in compliance with established policies and procedures and reconciles University Credit Card and serves as point-of-contact for ordering commodity items and ensures departmental purchases are in compliance with established policies and procedures. May reconcile the University Credit Card. Provides administrative support to the department that includes staffing the front desk and greeting guests as needed. Distributes mail and faxes as needed. Answers incoming calls and provides assistance and information to callers. Assists in managing the compliance email accounts. Provides other office support as needed. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two (2) years of office or related experience providing administrative support, or coordinating functions of an office or department; OR six (6) years of office or related experience; OR an equivalent combination of relevant education and/or experience. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $42,000 - $49,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Expanded Background Check How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. Disclosures Clery Notice In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act , the University Police department at Florida International University provides information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three (3) calendar years. The FIU Annual Security report is available online at: https://police.fiu.edu/download/annual-security-fire-safety-report/ . To obtain a paper copy of the report, please visit the FIU Police Department located at 885 SW 109th Avenue, Miami, FL, 33199 (PG5 Market Station). Pay Transparency Florida International University will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or (c) consistent with the contractor's legal duty to furnish information. Notice of Non-Discrimination FIU is a State University System of Florida member, Equal Opportunity, Equal Access, and Affirmative Action Employer for individuals with disabilities and veterans. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment decisions, programs, and events without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, and any other legally protected basis. For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination, contact FIU's Office of Title IX and EEO Compliance (TITLEIX) at 305.348.2785 or email titleix@fiu.edu. Reasonable Accommodation Statement Should you need an ADA accommodation to participate in a University event, program, or activity or need to request materials in an accessible format, please contact the Office of Universal Access