      "title": "Social Media Student Assistant",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-16 Department: Marketing and New Media College: Marketing & Strategic Communications Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Social Media Student Assistant will support the social media team in content creation, campaign execution, and platform management to enhance FIU's digital presence. Duties: Assist in developing and producing content across social platforms. Contribute to campaign ideation and creative briefs. Support brainstorming sessions and social media calendar planning. Assist with video production and photography concepts. Edit photo and video content for social use. Support on-site shoots, events, and brand activation as needed. Draft and refine social media copy aligned with FIU's brand voice. Design visual content that drives engagement and awareness. Monitor community engagement across platforms. Track and report on key social media metrics. Conduct competitive analysis across peer institutions. Monitor industry trends and maintain a library of content ideas and practices. Contribute to weekly and monthly insights reporting. Minimum Qualifications Ability to work in a team setting. Intermediate level of Microsoft Word and Excel. Knowledge of PC operations and specialized software. Ability to take direction and work independently as needed. Ability to maintain confidentiality when dealing with highly sensitive information. Job Category Student Assistant Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must end. Work Schedule 20hrs per week Advertised Salary $14.00/hour to $15.00/hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and 