      "title": "Student eSports Program Assistant",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-15 Department: Student Life and Development College: Division of Student Affairs Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary Job Summary The eSports Varsity & Competition Student Program Assistant provides operational, administrative, and programmatic support for FIU eSports varsity teams and competitive gaming initiatives. This position assists with competition logistics, compliance, scheduling, communication, and team coordination to help ensure FIU varsity teams are well-prepared for successful participation in collegiate esports competitions. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Assist in ensuring FIU eSports varsity teams are prepared for competition and operate in compliance with applicable National Association of Collegiate eSports (NACE) regulations, policies, and competition requirements. Support the maintenance of competition schedules, team rosters, player eligibility records, rankings, and other materials necessary for varsity competition operations. Coordinate and confirm reservations for the eSports Lounge and other designated competition spaces, ensuring facilities, equipment, and technology are prepared for scheduled events and matches. Monitor national rankings across FIU varsity esports titles and provide regular updates to the eSports Committee and departmental leadership. Assist with communication and coordination between student competitors, coaches, staff, and external esports organizations. Support match-day operations, including competition setup, check-in procedures, technology readiness, and troubleshooting basic logistical issues. Maintain accurate records related to competitions, team participation, and program outcomes. Assist with the development of reports, assessments, and program evaluations to support continuous improvement of varsity esports operations. Provide administrative and customer service support for esports programs, events, and initiatives. Minimum Qualifications Requires prior completion of FIU Service Excellence training or completion within first 30 days. Ability to work in a team setting. Intermediate level of Microsoft Word and Excel. Knowledge of PC operations and specialized software. Ability to take direction and work independently as needed. Ability to maintain confidentiality when dealing with highly sensitive information. Job Category Student Assistant Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must end. Work Schedule Up to 20 hours per week Advertised Salary $15.00/hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a 