      "title": "Senior Coordinator Administrative Services - College of Public Health & Social Work",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-15 Department: CPHSW Environmental Health Sci College: Robert Stempel College of Public Health and Social Work Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary Under administrative direction, the Senior Coordinator of Administrative Services provides administrative coordination and operational support for the Center for Advancing Personalized Cancer Treatments (CAPCT) and helps keep the unit's day-to-day functions running smoothly. The position serves as a central point of contact for vendor relationships and equipment delivery and installation logistics that support the Center's research and clinical operations, ensures that regulatory and compliance documentation is accurate and current, and monitors the progress of departmental projects from planning through completion. Drawing on knowledge of business administration and office practices and procedures, the incumbent carries out moderately complex assignments in support of the Center's operations, prepares reports and correspondence, and assists the department head and staff with scheduling, budget-related matters, and recordkeeping. Coordinates project-oriented activities for the Center, including planning, initiation, implementation, and evaluation, and tracks milestones, deliverables, and reporting deadlines through completion. Serves as the primary point of contact for vendors; establishes and maintains ongoing communication and follows up on quotes, orders, and service matters. Coordinates the logistics of equipment delivery and installation, scheduling deliveries and confirming that installations are completed as planned. Maintains regulatory and compliance documentation, ensuring records are accurate, complete, organized, and current. Composes and prepares correspondence, memoranda, forms, newsletters, manuals, and reports using appropriate word processing and spreadsheet applications. Prepares presentation and reference materials for use by department staff and leadership. Performs basic statistical calculations and compiles data for reports and presentations. Plans, prioritizes, and schedules meetings and appointments, and maintains calendars for the department. Assists and advises the department head and staff, as needed, on budgetary and related operational matters. Organizes and maintains confidential files and departmental records. Performs other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree and three (3) years of office or related experience providing administrative support, or coordinating functions of an office or department; OR seven (7) years of office or related experience; OR an equivalent combination of relevant education and/or experience. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $60,000 - $65,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check Other Information This position is funded by an external funding source (e.g. a grant or contract). How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, 