      "title": "Donor Stewardship Officer I",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-15 Department: Donor Relations College: Advancement Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Donor Relations & Stewardship Officer I is responsible for personalized donor impact reporting including but not limited to endowment reporting and scholarship reporting sent on behalf of the FIU Foundation. Manages the administrative functions of the Office of Donor Relations and Stewardship, including schedules, meetings, and official functions hosted by the department. Conducts correspondence, research, and reports. Serves as the department point person for process management of the annual endowment reporting cycle. Utilizes data to draft and edit the stewardship and recognition correspondence and reports both on a one-to-one basis and one-to-many. Serves as liaison to academic units, providing assistance, and coordination on recognition, stewardship, and cultivation activities within the University. Assists the Director of Donor Relations and Stewardship in implementing donor relations and stewardship programs for the University as well as individualized stewardship plans for donors. Assists the Director of Donor Relations and Stewardship in assessing donors with a potential to provide additional funding, establishing a stewardship/cultivation approach which may additionally provide financial support to the University. Maintains frequent communication and contact with prospects, donors, university executives and leaders in the community on behalf of the Office of Donor Relations and Stewardship. Represents the Office of Donor Relations and Stewardship at public functions as needed. Maintains prospect and donor data at the highest level of confidentiality. Interprets and implements policies and procedures as they apply to an assigned area. May recommend changes on policy and procedures as necessary. May supervise lower level staff. Performs related duties as required or as directed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree and one (1) year of experience writing and editing letters or other types of correspondence; OR five (5) years of experience writing and editing letters or other types of correspondence; OR an equivalent combination of relevant education and/or experience. Desired Qualifications Proficiency with donor relationship management (CRM) software, particularly Blackbaud Raiser's Edge NXT, Salesforce, or similar platforms. Demonstrated experience with data entry, extraction, and reporting within a donor database. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $50,000 - $55,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Expanded Background Check Other Information Must attend meetings off campus and occasionally attend functions on weekends and evening Ability to work flexible hours as needed. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a 