      "title": "Staff Writer",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-02-09 Department: Media Relations College: Marketing & Strategic Communications Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Staff Writer in the Executive Communications team assists the Director of Communications and the President's speechwriter in crafting and delivering compelling written content that resonates with a wide range of audiences, including students, faculty, staff, alumni, and community supporters. This position requires a creative, detail-oriented writer who understands the importance of tone, voice, and accuracy. Conducts research and produces an array of content in both English and Spanish, such as talking points, remarks, internal memos, and various communications for executives and the university community. Collaborates closely with the Director of Communications and President's speechwriter to understand the specific needs for each assignment. Conducts research to ensure accuracy and relevancy of the content. Works with tight deadlines while maintaining high standards of quality and consistency. Revises and edits drafts based on feedback from leaders and other stakeholders. Assists in maintaining the executive communication team's calendar and managing workflow. Performs other related duties as required or as directed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. *** IF YOU DO NOT SUBMIT A PROFESSIONAL PORTFOLIO OR RELEVANT WORK SAMPLES UPON APPLYING, YOU WILL NOT BE CONSDIERED*** Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree. Departmental Requirements Submission of a professional portfolio or relevant work samples is required upon application. Desired Qualifications Experience in a university setting or understanding of higher education landscape. Familiarity with content management systems. Spanish writing skills preferred. Ability to adapt writing style to suit different audiences and media. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $45,000 - $50,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including 