      "title": "Student entry level",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-19 Department: Gov't & Community Relations College: Government & Community Relations Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Office of Government, Corporate, and Community Relations at FIU is seeking an energetic Student Office Assistant to join the team. Duties and Responsibilities Perform office support including copying, scanning, sorting mail, and filing documents. Input basic data into spreadsheets and departmental logs. Run campus errands such as delivering documents to other university departments. Organize office spaces and track inventories of event materials or office supplies. Provide basic support for the coordination of upcoming community and corporate events. Complete required training programs including FIU Cyber Security and Service Excellence within 30 days of hire. Minimum Qualifications Must be a currently enrolled FIU student . Registered for a minimum of 6 credits (Undergraduate) or 3 credits (Graduate). Possess basic knowledge of Microsoft Word, Outlook, and Excel. Ability to take direction well and execute tasks independently. Ability to maintain high confidentiality when handling sensitive information. Preferred Skills Strong verbal and written communication skills . Keen interest in public relations, community affairs , or government relations. High sense of responsibility and attention to detail . Minimum Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Must be a currently enrolled FIU student . Registered for a minimum of 6 credits (Undergraduate) or 3 credits (Graduate). Possess basic knowledge of Microsoft Word, Outlook, and Excel. Ability to take direction well and execute tasks independently. Ability to maintain high confidentiality when handling sensitive information. Job Category Student Assistant Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must end. Work Schedule Up to 20 hours per week maximum. Exact daily schedule to be determined with the department upon hire. Advertised Salary $14.00/hour to $15.00/hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performan