      "title": "Student Program Assistant- Relay for Life",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-16 Department: Center for Leadership SA College: Division of Student Affairs Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Center for Leadership and Service (CLS) is seeking a motivated, detail-oriented, and enthusiastic individual to support the Relay for Life program. This position will assist with the coordination of program logistics, administrative tasks, and event support to ensure a successful Relay for Life experience for students and the campus community. The Student Program Assistant will work closely with staff, volunteers, and the Relay for Life Executive Board to provide behind-the-scenes support while also engaging with participants and partners. Minimum Qualifications Provide administrative and logistical support for Relay for Life, including scheduling meetings, preparing agendas, and maintaining attendance/records. Assist with program communications such as e-mails, phone calls, and social media updates. Support committee chair and student leaders by helping track deadlines, goals, and progress. Coordinate program materials, supplies, and event-day logistics. Maintain and update databases, spreadsheets, and participation records. Assist with planning and execution of team captain meetings, fundraising trainings, and other pre-event activities. Help facilitate volunteer recognition efforts through thank-you notes, acknowledgements, and appreciation initiatives. Serve as a point of contact for students, faculty, staff, and partners who inquire about the program. Provide excellent customer service and represent the Center for Leadership and Service at events and meetings. Desired Qualifications Strong organizational and time-management skills. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a team setting. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Excel and other Office applications. Previous event planning or program support experience preferred. Available to work at least 10 hours per week. Job Category Student Assistant Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must end. Work Schedule Monday through Friday 20 hours a week. Advertised Salary $15.00/hour Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check This student appointment may be subjected to a pre-employment background check. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \