 and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. Pre-Employment Requirements Advertised Salary $20 per hour Work Schedule 20 Hours Temporary Disclosure As a temporary employee, you will not be eligible to participate in all employee benefit programs (e.g., paid leave, retirement, or tuition reimbursement). Under the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (PPACA), a temporary employee who works on average 30 hours or more per week may be eligible to enroll in health care benefits. As a temporary employee, you are also eligible to enroll in supplemental plans (e.g. dental, vision,) which requires full payment on your part. Upon completing an assignment, employees may apply for a position on FIU Careers. Desired Qualifications 1. Some college coursework in health services administration, healthcare management, education, instructional technology, or a related field. An associate or bachelor's degree is preferred but not required. 2. At least one year of experience with online learning, whether as an online student or in instructional design, academic support, or academic administration. 3. Working knowledge of a learning management system, preferably Canvas. 4. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite. 5. Advanced proficiency in Canva. 6. Familiarity with PC operations and specialized software. 7. Ability to maintain confidentiality when handling sensitive information, including student records protected under FERPA. 8. Ability to follow direction, work independently, and solve problems with minimal supervision. 9. Ability to work effectively as part of a team. 10. Clear, concise verbal and written communication skills. 11. Strong sense of responsibility and customer service. 12. Strong organizational and time management skills. Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or GED and five (5) years of office or related experience providing administrative support, or coordinating functions of an office or department. Job Summary 1. Assist faculty with creating and updating course materials, including syllabi, reading lists, and lecture slides. 2. Assist with course setup in Canvas, including locating and adding relevant content, such as articles, videos, and interactive resources, that promotes student engagement. 3. Help maintain assigned Canvas courses by keeping non content materials current, such as syllabi, schedules, and administrative announcements. 4. Post announcements and reminders about deadlines and submission processes. 5. Support course improvement efforts by distributing midterm surveys, setting up online questionnaires, gathering student feedback, and sharing results with faculty. 6. Help monitor end of semester course evaluations and encourage student participation to reach target response rates. 7. Curate and organize course related resources, including academic materials, software tools, and databases, to support student research. 8. Help organize workshops on academic writing, presentation skills, and software proficiency each academic term. 9. Assist faculty with grading assignments using course approved rubrics, and provide student feedback within one week of submission. Job Category Temporary"
    },
    "https://pslinks.fiu.edu/psc/jobs/CUSTOMER/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST&Action=U&JobOpeningId=538355&postingseq=1&SiteId=1000&REL_ACTION=Yes": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Admissions - Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-20 Department: COM Academic Affairs College: Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine is currently seeking an Assistant Director of Admissions to join our team of professionals. Duties include: Oversees the admissions process for the Master in Physician Assistant Studies (MPAS) program, including the scheduling of interviews and applicant communication. Serves as the liaison between prospective students and university departments, providing guidance and mentorship throughout the admissions process. Reviews and evaluates applications submitted through the Centralized Application Service for Physician Assistants (CASPA). Maintains interview documentation and creates admission records for accepted students, including all pre-matriculation materials. Prepares admissions reports by gathering, analyzing, and summarizing data and trends to support informed decision-making by MPAS leadership. Develops recruitment strategies focused on attracting and engaging prospective applicants. Collaborates with the Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine (HWCOM) marketing team to develop promotional materials. Develops, implements, and participates in recruitment events, including monthly information sessions, campus tours, and college fairs. Conducts special presentations for Pre-PA and Pre-Health organizations, as requested. Drives to FIU campuses and travels, as needed. Conducts and records prerequisite equivalency reviews. Maintains MPAS repository with updated course descriptions and syllabi. Manages student inquiries related to student support services available at FIU. Provides detailed guidance to students on complex issues involving institutional policies, procedures, and state/federal regulations. Collaborates with the University Graduate School, Office of Financial Aid, Pre-Health Advising, and external vendors (e.g., CASPA, Exam Master PA-CAT) to ensure effective admissions and matriculation processes. Validates all matriculated and enrolled student immunization credentials. Communicates with prospective and enrolled students regarding deficiencies in compliance requirements, in collaboration with HWCOM's Director of Compliance and the MPAS Clinical Team Leads the planning and coordination of departmental initiatives and student engagement activities, to include: Meet and Greet events, Orientation, White Coat Ceremony, Awards and Graduation Ceremony, and alumni socials. Develops student policies and matriculation procedures for the MPAS Student Handbook, ensuring compliance with the rules and regulations set forth by FIU, HWCOM, ARC-PA, the State and Federal government. Updates admissions policies and deadlines on the program's webpage. Facilitates and processes graduate verification forms required for physician assistant licensure in collaboration with HWCOM's Registrar. Maintains accurate records on file. Collaborates with COM's Student Affairs Registrars in the student matriculation, course creation, and registration in PantherSoft (PS). Plans and coordinates meetings for the Admissions Committee (AC) and Student Evaluation and Progress Committee (SEPC). Prepares meeting materials as directed by the Committee Chair(s) and maintains records, including minutes and student correspondence. Coordinates the maintenance and permanent security of each matriculated MPAS student's official academic record including official documents pertaining to student promotion, disciplinary actions, leaves of absence, withdrawals, and other changes in student status. Monitors and updates Panther Degree Audit (PDA) for each student. Maintains the Student Affairs course shell on CanvasMed and manages the program's social media accounts. Provides students and alumni with routine updates on programmatic events and job opportunities. Collaborates with HWCOM's Assistant Director of Alumni Relations to strengthen alumni engagement and cultivate long-term affinity with the program. Manages the MPAS department email account and triages incoming phone calls from the department's main line. Serves as an active member of the Admissions and Accreditation committees. Performs other duties as assigned or directed by the supervisor. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's and six (6) years of related experience OR Master's degree and four (4) years of related experience OR a JD and two (2) years of experience. Desired Qualifications Knowledge of College organization: admission, registration, academic regulations, programs of study and departmental regulations. Knowledge of College activities and special programs, college regulations, testing, counseling and advisement services. Ability to write routine reports and correspondence. Ability to speak effectively before groups of customers or employees of organization. Ability to maintain effective interpersonal relations with students, faculty and administration. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $65,000 - $67,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. Disclosures Clery Notice In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act , the University Police department at Florida International University provides information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three (3) calendar years. The FIU Annual Security report is available online at: https://police.fiu.edu/download/annual-security-fire-safety-report/ . To obtain a paper copy of the report, please visit the FIU Police Department located at 885 SW 109th Avenue, Miami, FL, 33199 (PG5 Market Station). Pay Transparency Florida International University will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or (c) consistent with the contractor's legal duty to furnish information. Notice of Non-Discrimination FIU is a State University System of Florida member, Equal Opportunity, Equal Access, and Affirmative Action Employer for individuals with disabilities and veterans. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment decisions, programs, and events without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, and any other legally protected basis. For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination, contact FIU's Office of Title IX and EEO Compliance (TITLEIX) at 305.348.2785 or email titleix@fiu.edu. Reasonable Accommodation Statement Should you need an ADA accommodation to participate in a University event, program, or activity or need to request materials in an accessible format, please contact the Office of Universal Access and Digital Compliance at 305-348-1576 or accommodations@fiu.edu. All requests for ADA accommodation or accessible materials for this event must be submitted to UADC at least seven (7) business days prior to the event or at the earliest possible opportunity."
