      "title": "IT Multimedia Producer",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-22 Department: IT Media Technology Support College: Division of Information Technology Job family: Staff Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary Performs and organizes the digitization / digital imaging activities for the office. Operates video cameras in studio and at remote locations. Sets up lighting, teleprompter, microphones and other audio equipment as required. Executes post-production operations including audio, video, graphics creation, special effects and voice over. Performs photography services at various university events; responsible for post-production including editing, and delivery of high quality images. Operates lecture capture and video conference equipment, including switchers, cameras, audio/video appliances, computers and software. Serves as a consultant to faculty, staff and students in the design, production and utilization of digital images for classroom, research, training or promotional purposes. Recommends the most appropriate equipment, lighting and accessories. Acts as director at production of events when multiple cameras and crew is required, selects and recruit team, selects and prepare equipment, supervises and participate in equipment setups, directs the event, performs or assign post-production tasks, plans deliverables, plans deadlines and is responsible for final product results. Produces videos for faculty and staff for instructional, research, administrative, public relations and promotional purposes and is responsible for final product results. Trains and supervises temporary personnel in the correct use of equipment, in addition to industry and university standards and procedures. Verifies the correct functioning of the equipment and maintains and troubleshoot equipment when required. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in related field and two (2) years of experience in related field; OR six (6) years of experience in a related field; OR an equivalent combination of relevant education and/or experience. Desired Qualifications Experience providing IT support to events and/or classrooms. Ability to push/pull/lift Audio-Visual equipment. Job Category Staff Advertised Salary $40,000 - $45,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Working Condition(s) Operating University Vehicles (all types). Must carry/lift up to 50 lbs. Pre-Employment Requirements Driver's License Check Expanded Background Check Other Information Ability to work evenings and weekends. Ability to travel locally and nationally. Ability to work flexible hours as needed. Travel to FIU Campus. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must 