    "https://pslinks.fiu.edu/psc/jobs/CUSTOMER/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST&Action=U&JobOpeningId=538384&postingseq=1&SiteId=1000&REL_ACTION=Yes": {
      "title": "Accounting Manager",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-22 Department: FIU Foundation College: Advancement Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary Manages daily accounting and reporting activities, in assigned areas, for FIU Foundation. Assists the Controller and Assistant Controller with developing and implementing accounting procedures to improve compliance with institutional and Federal/State regulations. Establishes, interprets, and analyzes complex accounting functions. Analyzes, balances and researches financial data discrepancies. Manages and coordinates daily accounting functions of the FIU Foundation, Inc. of Florida International University by creating detailed schedules, financial analysis of accounts and transactions. Creates required notes disclosures to the Audited Financial Statements. Reviews accounting and reporting environment to look for opportunities to create and/or enhance efficiencies in reporting and the reporting process. Researches new accounting pronouncements to determine their applicability to the Foundation. Assists the Controller in interpreting and implementing new accounting pronouncements which may include developing new reports and/or schedules. Assists the Controller with special projects. Prepares and reviews reconciliations of accounts and subledgers, journal entries, supporting schedules and other work papers, as well as analyzes balances and researches discrepancies in financial data as they related to the assigned areas of responsibility. Responsible for reviewing and analyzing the pledge receivables for Foundation, including but not limited to write offs, adjustments, and past due pledges to create accounting entries, adjustments, and supporting audit schedules and summaries The analysis serves to assist management in reviewing key metrics, trends and to inform decision making. Coordinates with various departments to review and establish new Foundation projects. Creates letter of agreements with the Office of Research and Economic Development for projects which involve research Serves as primary liaison between the Foundation and Office of Research and Economic Development for related compliance matters, no cost and cost extensions on projects, application and development of policies and procedures, etc. Works with the University community and outside constituents to develop and implement strategies, procedures and processes based on best practices to improve customer service standards. Responds to and resolves issues efficiently and effectively. Provides leadership for customer service delivery consistent with the goals and objectives of the University, including, training on the creation of new projects, including research projects, for the University community . May assist with the preparation and review of quarterly and annual financial reports, summaries and analysis for tracking metrics, trends and providing ad hoc information to management.. Responsible for overseeing the reconciliation of Revenue Suspense on a monthly basis. Responsible for reviewing and posting any journal entries to reclass donations from revenue suspense to newly established project in accordance with donor intent once proper documentation is received. Oversees and directs the maintainances and updating of the summary of project descriptions and project support as needed, due to new projects setup, amendments to gift agreements, ORED letter of agreements and budget modifications, completed reports, or other documentation. Oversees the process for documenting any life insurance policies in which Foundation is owner and beneficiary. Update any documentation and issue premium payment(s) to life insurance company, as needed. Communicate with development team any past due/unpaid pledge installments for follow up with donor(s). Works with various University departments/units and Foundation team to review the required in-take forms when event proceeds will be received by the Foundation. Works with Gift Compliance & Administration department to review any gift agreements which have various financial calculations, such as gift fee, budgets, etc. Performs related duties as required or as directed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Accounting or related business field, to include a minimum of 6 credits in Accounting, and six (6) years of directly-related experience; OR Master's degree in Accounting or related business field, or an MBA and four (4) years of directly-related experience. Desired Qualifications Non-profit and GASB Accounting experience. Experience with financial statement preparation. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $73,000 - $75,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check Other Information Ability to work flexible hours as needed. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. Disclosures Clery Notice In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act , the University Police department at Florida International University provides information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three (3) calendar years. The FIU Annual Security report is available online at: https://police.fiu.edu/download/annual-security-fire-safety-report/ . To obtain a paper copy of the report, please visit the FIU Police Department located at 885 SW 109th Avenue, Miami, FL, 33199 (PG5 Market Station). Pay Transparency Florida International University will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or (c) consistent with the contractor's legal duty to furnish information. Notice of Non-Discrimination FIU is a State University System of Florida member, Equal Opportunity, Equal Access, and Affirmative Action Employer for individuals with disabilities and veterans. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment decisions, programs, and events without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, and any other legally protected basis. For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination, contact FIU's Office of Title IX and EEO Compliance (TITLEIX) at 305.348.2785 or email titleix@fiu.edu. Reasonable Accommodation Statement Should you need an ADA accommodation to participate in a University event, program, or activity or need to request materials in an accessible format, please contact the Office of Universal Access and Digital Compliance at 305-348-1576 or accommodations@fiu.edu. All requests for ADA accommodation or accessible materials for this event must be submitted to UADC at least seven (7) business days prior to the event or at the earliest possible opportunity."
