      "title": "Coordinator Academic Support Services",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-22 Department: Transfer and Transition Svcs College: Enrollment Services Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary Responsible for the daily management of the Transfer and Transition Services (TTS) equivalency, flent/flex (Foreign Language State Requirement), and accelerated credits intake process. Liaises between TTS and FIU Academic Advisement Leads, Advisors, EMS and Student Affairs staff in issues relating to transfer students and accelerated credits. Assists the Director of Transfer & Transition Services with the management of the department and its operational duties. Manages the intake process and assignment of student generated course equivalency process for transfers. Responsible for tracking, recording and reporting data as it pertains to this intake process. Records and analyses the outcomes of new initiatives and reports them to Director of TTS. Ensures compliance with FIU policies, procedures, practices and programs, and with federal, state and local legal/regulatory standards, for example, (FERPA) are followed by employees. Manages the escalated complex requests from the front line staff. Assists in the administration and interpretation of FIU transfer credit policies, state laws, FIU procedures and communicates those accordingly. Acts as a liaison between TTS and Academic Units, EMS Departments, Student Affairs Departments and Academic and Career Success in order to meet departmental strategies and goals. Researches and resolves complex programming issues in relation to Peoplesoft and the transfer test credit, equivalency or transfer credit processes. Works together with the TTS team and Business Analyst to find solutions to problems. Analyzes glitches and rare cases in Peoplesoft. Responsible for reporting these to the EMS Business Analyst and working in conjunction to strategize solutions. Responsible for managing all the social media accounts for the department. Reviews contents and manages the reporting of the social media analytics for the department. Manages special events including planning, initiating, coordinating and implementing for office events such as: Transfer meet and greet events, Transfer Orientation, Admissions Presentation among others. Supervises departmental Student Assistants and Federal Work Study (FWS) employees. Responsible for coordinating weekly work schedules, training and finding replacements when vacancies occur. Performs other related duties as assigned or as directed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two (2) years of appropriate experience, or Master's degree. Desired Qualifications Intermediate knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite. Experience with PeopleSoft. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $40,000-$43,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Working Condition(s) Required to spend 50% or more of time operating a computer Pre-Employment Requirements Expanded 