      "title": "Student Operations Assistant - Graham Center",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-23 Department: Graham Center College: Division of Student Affairs Job family: Student Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Graham Center (GC) at Florida International University seeks dedicated Student Operations Assistants to join our dynamic team. This role offers the opportunity to contribute to the smooth operations and positive atmosphere of the Graham Center by providing essential support in maintaining our facilities and assisting with event logistics. With a focus on delivering high-quality service to all GC guests, the Student Operations Assistant is a vital member of our professional team. Key Responsibilities: Facility Maintenance and Cleanliness: Proactively clean meeting, event, and general spaces to uphold the GC's standards for cleanliness and orderliness. This includes vacuuming, mopping, cleaning tables and chairs, and changing trash. Event and Meeting Support: Assist with the set-up and breakdown of meetings and events, ensuring spaces are prepared according to specific needs and timelines. This includes the set-up and breakdown of staging, dance floors, tables, chairs, pipe, drape, etc. Safety Reporting: Actively report any safety and security concerns to the appropriate personnel, contributing to the overall safety of the GC environment. Team Collaboration: Work closely with the custodial team and other GC staff members to deliver seamless facility operations and event support. Customer Service: Provide friendly and professional customer service to all GC guests and customers, ensuring their needs are met promptly and effectively. Additional Support: Assist GC leadership as required, demonstrating initiative and problem-solving abilities Job Category Student Assistant Student Disclosure Applicants must be currently enrolled as a student at FIU with a minimum of six (6) credits as an Undergraduate student or three (3) credits as a Graduate student during the Fall and Spring semesters. During the Summer semesters, Students need only remain enrolled and are not required to take credit hours, but cannot have graduated. Upon decreasing credit hours or graduating, student employment must end. Work Schedule Flexible schedule based on facility needs and hours of operations. Up to 20 hours a week. Advertised Salary $15.00/hour How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF for