      "title": "Open Rank Tenure Track, Faculty Position in Sport and Recreation Management",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-26 Department: Counseling Rec and Schl Psych College: College of Arts, Sciences and Education Job family: Faculty Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Information Open Rank Tenure Track Faculty Position in Sport and Recreation Management The Department of Counseling, Recreation and School Psychology (CRSP) in the College of Arts, Sciences & Education at Florida International University invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-earning open rank faculty position in Sport and Recreation Management, anticipated to begin in Fall 2027. Responsibilities ' Develop and sustain a productive research agenda in sport and recreation management or a closely related field, including dissemination through peer-reviewed scholarship and pursuit of external funding, as appropriate. ' Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Sport and Recreation Management in face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online formats, consistent with program and departmental needs. ' Mentor and advise undergraduate and graduate students, including support for academic progression, career development, research participation, and professional preparation. ' Contribute to curriculum development, assessment of student learning, program planning, and continuous improvement. ' Engage in service to the department, college, university, profession, and community consistent with the expectations for a tenure-earning faculty appointment. ' Establish and strengthen partnerships with sport, recreation, wellness, community, municipal, nonprofit, and industry organizations that enhance research, experiential learning, and student career opportunities. ' Collaborate across FIU in areas relevant to health, technology and innovation, community wellbeing, sport, recreation, events, analytics, or related interdisciplinary priorities. Minimum Qualifications ' An earned doctorate in Sport Management, Recreation Management, Leisure Studies, Kinesiology, Sport Business, Public Health, Event Management, or a closely related discipline by the time of appointment. ' Evidence of, or clear potential for, a focused and productive research agenda in sport and recreation management or a related area. ' Evidence of, or potential for, effective university-level teaching. ' Demonstrated ability or potential to work effectively with students, colleagues, and community partners from a wide range of backgrounds. ' Excellent written, oral, interpersonal, and organizational communication skills. Preferred Qualifications ' Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate one or more of the following: ' A record of peer-reviewed publications, presentations, grant activity, or evidence of potential for externally supported research. ' Expertise in areas such as sport business; sport governance; sport analytics; sport technology; sport marketing and consumer behavior; youth sport; recreation and community development; health and wellness; community engagement in sport and recreation; event, venue, or facility management; tourism and sport; or related areas. ' Experience with community-engaged, interdisciplinary, or applied research. ' Experience teaching in multiple instructional formats, including online or hybrid education. ' Professional or industry experience relevant to sport and recreation management. ' Evidence of successful student mentoring, curriculum development, assessment, or partnership building. About the Program The Sport and Recreation Management Program is a vibrant and growing program with a healthy number of applicants and strong enrollment. It is situated within the Department of Counseling, Recreation, and School Psychology in the School of Education and Human Development at the College of Arts, Sciences, & Education (CASE). SRM undergraduate enrollment increased from 280 students in 2023'24 to 311 students in 2024'25 and 337 students in 2025'26, a 20.4% increase over two years. The program seeks a tenure-earning faculty member who will help translate this growth into enduring academic quality, student success, research productivity, and regional engagement. For undergraduate information, please visit: BS in Sport and Recreation Management, and for graduate information, visit: MS Sport and Recreation Management. Qualified candidates are encouraged to apply to Job Opening ID 538438 at careers.fiu.edu and attach a cover letter, a CV, a teaching philosophy statement, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and transcripts. Candidates will be requested to provide names and contact information for at least three (3) references who will be contacted as determined by the search committee. To receive full consideration, applications and required materials should be received by 11/25/2026. The review will continue until the position is filled. Please direct any questions to Hyejin Bang at bangh@fiu.edu. Job Category Faculty Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. Disclosures Clery Notice In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act , the University Police department at Florida International University provides information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three (3) calendar years. The FIU Annual Security report is available online at: https://police.fiu.edu/download/annual-security-fire-safety-report/ . To obtain a paper copy of the report, please visit the FIU Police Department located at 885 SW 109th Avenue, Miami, FL, 33199 (PG5 Market Station). Pay Transparency Florida International University will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or (c) consistent with the contractor's legal duty to furnish information. Notice of Non-Discrimination FIU is a State University System of Florida member, Equal Opportunity, Equal Access, and Affirmative Action Employer for individuals with disabilities and veterans. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment decisions, programs, and events without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, and any other legally protected basis. For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination, contact FIU's Office of Title IX and EEO Compliance (TITLEIX) at 305.348.2785 or email titleix@fiu.edu. Reasonable Accommodation Statement Should you need an ADA accommodation to participate in a University event, program, or activity or need to request materials in an accessible format, please contact the Office of Universal Access and Digital Compliance at 305-348-1576 or accommodations@fiu.edu. All requests for ADA accommodation or accessible materials for this event must be submitted to UADC at least seven (7) business days prior to the event or at the earliest possible opportunity."
