      "title": "Office Specialist - Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-27 Department: COM Clinical Affairs College: Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine Job family: Staff Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine is currently seeking a Office Specialist to join our team of professionals Duties: Organizes various Educational Seminar Series, Faculty Meetings, and other educational meetings. Provides Continuing Medical Education (CME) applications and finance & travel documentation to speakers. Ensures biography, photo and any other documentation is received, completed in its entirety, and forwarded to respective departments. Composes and/or prepares a wide variety of materials and presentations for the assigned department faculty and staff. Edits content and adds appropriate graphic and design elements. Performs clerical duties to include answering telephone calls, filing and data entry. Assists with internet research, compiling data and creating spreadsheets. Assists with scheduling and coordinating conferences, meetings, appointments, and travel arrangements for assigned department faculty and clinical staff. Creates save the dates, notifications, invitations, agendas, list of attendees, and coordinates catering orders for all educational meetings. Creates, processes and tracks departmental purchases in respect to educational initiatives and for assigned faculty and clinical staff. Creates student schedules for the psychiatry rotation for both International Medical Students and Master in Physician Assistant Studies programs. Organizes the Psychiatry Observed Interviews and meetings for the medical students who are interested in psychiatry. Ensures meeting calendar invites are up to par and confirms meetings appointments prior to day of scheduled meeting. Maintains records of orders and inventory and follows up with vendors on shipment and delivery for educational initiatives. Maintains strong relationships with faculty and staff by handling questions and concerns with speed and professionalism. Travels to The Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Health (DOPBH) affiliated sites Performs other related duties as required or as directed. The omission of specific duties do not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Works directly with and/or resides with minors and/or vulnerable persons. Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or GED and four (4) years office or related experience providing administrative support, or coordinating functions of an office or department; OR an equivalent combination of relevant education and/or experience. Desired Qualifications Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends and able to travel to FIU campuses and affiliated hospitals. Job Category Staff Advertised Salary $33,000 - $35,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Fingerprinting Check Expanded Background Check How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for 