compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or (c) consistent with the contractor's legal duty to furnish information. Notice of Non-Discrimination FIU is a State University System of Florida member, Equal Opportunity, Equal Access, and Affirmative Action Employer for individuals with disabilities and veterans. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment decisions, programs, and events without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, and any other legally protected basis. For inquiries regarding nondiscrimination, contact FIU's Office of Title IX and EEO Compliance (TITLEIX) at 305.348.2785 or email titleix@fiu.edu. Reasonable Accommodation Statement Should you need an ADA accommodation to participate in a University event, program, or activity or need to request materials in an accessible format, please contact the Office of Universal Access and Digital Compliance at 305-348-1576 or accommodations@fiu.edu. All requests for ADA accommodation or accessible materials for this event must be submitted to UADC at least seven (7) business days prior to the event or at the earliest possible opportunity. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. Pre-Employment Requirements Advertised Salary $15.00 Work Schedule 8:30am - 5pm 1 Year 35 Hours Temporary Disclosure As a temporary employee, you will not be eligible to participate in all employee benefit programs (e.g., paid leave, retirement, or tuition reimbursement). Under the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (PPACA), a temporary employee who works on average 30 hours or more per week may be eligible to enroll in health care benefits. As a temporary employee, you are also eligible to enroll in supplemental plans (e.g. dental, vision,) which requires full payment on your part. Upon completing an assignment, employees may apply for a position on FIU Careers. Job Category Temporary Minimum Qualifications High School diploma and two (2) years of related work experience. Job Summary The Visitor Service Associate creates an enhanced visitor experience at the museum; greets visitors enthusiastically and shares knowledge about the museum. Performs clerical tasks and processes a variety of sales in point of sale system. Maintains overall appearance of museum entrance and assists during museum events. Schedules, trains and supervises temporary employees and interns. Develops and implements effective initiatives and strategies to ensure consistent excellent customer service. -Greet visitors, share information about exhibitions, events, and collections, and resolve concerns professionally -Record daily visitor, tour, and event attendance and provide reports as requested -Answer the main phone line and email and route inquiries to appropriate staff -Conduct visitor surveys and report results as requested -Keep the entrance, front desk, and closet clean and organized and restock brochures -Track daily museum activities using Outlook calendars -Process sales, tickets, rentals, tours, donations, and memberships in the POS system following cash-handling procedures -Check the Kenan Flagler Family Discovery Gallery weekly, tidy as needed, and report technical issues to the Curator of Education and IT Specialist -Enter data into the contact database as directed -Assist with event setup and breakdown -Perform related duties as assigned"
    },
    "https://pslinks.fiu.edu/psc/jobs/CUSTOMER/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST&Action=U&JobOpeningId=538462&postingseq=1&SiteId=1000&REL_ACTION=Yes": {
      "title": "Program Specialist - Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-27 Department: COM Academic Affairs College: Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine Job family: Staff Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary The Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine is currently seeking a Program Specialist to join our team of professionals. Duties include: Assists in creating, editing, and maintaining of clerkship syllabi .Assists in sending and receiving clerkship, faculty, and student evaluation(s). Assists in tracking student attendance across affiliated hospitals or clinics. Assists in organizing and uploading documents in the system used by the Herbert Wertheim College of Medicine (HWCOM). Assists in scheduling students' clerkships and/or rotations. Updates a list of required and recommended textbooks or resources. Assists in planning for the successive calendar years. Participates in the preparation of Liaison Committee for Medical Education (LCME) accreditation materials. Schedules and coordinates meetings for faculty and clerkship directors with administration and affiliated hospitals or clinics. Confirms and updates the list of clinical faculty for each clerkship. Interacts with and assist students and faculty to find university information and comply with university policies and procedures. Assists Clerkship Coordinators in the preparation of materials for their clerkships e.g. copying, printing syllabi, collating documents. Performs related duties as required or as directed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or GED and 4 years of office or related experience coordinating functions of an office or department. Job Category Staff Advertised Salary $35,000 - $37,800 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your appli