      "title": "Senior HR Specialist",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-27 Department: College of Arts Science & Educ College: College of Arts, Sciences and Education Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary Assists with overseeing HR operations for the College of Arts, Sciences & Education (CASE) Dean's Office to include but not limited to faculty, admin, staff, Courtesy, POI and Volunteer appointment transactions for the School of Environment, Arts and Society (SEAS). Provides HR support to the College with an emphasis on implementation of policies. Provides general information to University constituents regarding HR programs, e.g. benefits, payroll, time/leave entry, and approval processes. Provides HR support to the College with an emphasis on implementation of policies. Provides immigration information and processes all immigration paperwork for faculty, admin, staff and Courtesy who are being sponsored by the College. Liaison with immigration coordinator and immigration attorney's office for these transactions. Process moving reimbursements. Works with central HR to process the payments through payroll. Interprets rules and policies and recommends new and improved programs to effectively manage the faculty, admin and staff with regards to human resources related issues. Uses discretion and independent judgement when working with the departments. Reviews assigned actions with the department and provides recommendations using best practices. May assist and provide backup for student/non student OPS, adjunct and federal work study appointment requests for the college. Serves as liaison between the Dean's office and assigned departments with regard to faculty, admin and staff HR issues. Coordinates and provides assistance with special projects; performs research, gathers and compiles data for preparation of various reports, documents, charts and graphs as needed. Assists with the maintenance of all college electronic HR files; including copies of all of the HR actions for the College. Performs related duties as assigned or as directed. The omission of specific duties does not preclude the supervisor from assigning duties that are logically related to the position. Works from the databases established in the college, generates change of status forms for faculty whose status has changed with the new academic year; moving from 9-month contract to 12-month contracts or vice-versa, , new employees (whether tenure-earning or visiting), receiving an administrative increments or increments being removed, going or returning from a leave of absence, appointed program director or stepping down, received a post-doc appointment or ending their post-doc appointment. Resolves all problems associated with incorrect information about faculty assignments submitted to the Dean's Office for assigned departments. Generates contracts for faculty whose assignment changed. Ensures faculty members are paid on a timely basis with Academic Budget and other University offices. Manages the paperwork associated with the recruitment and hiring of new faculty, admin and staff for assigned departments. Assists with the preparation of the offer letter and any subsequent revisions. Guides candidates upon arrival on campus and answers any questions prior to candidate's employment. Assists with the sign-on process and ensures necessary credentials are filed. Ensures information on faculty is accurate including, issues of change in rank, salary, assignments, designation as graduate faculty, dissertation advisor, or Honors fellow; addition or deletion of administrative increments, terms of appointment, receipt of University honors and awards, and change in unit status for assigned departments. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two (2) years of experience. Desired Qualifications Experience working with faculty. Experience working in Higher Education. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $50,000 - $55,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Working Condition(s) Required to spend 50% or more of time operating a computer Pre-Employment Requirements Criminal Background Check Other Information Ability to work flexible hours as needed. Travel to FIU Campus How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. All applicants are required to complete the online application including work history and educational details (if applicable), even when attaching a resume. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. Disclosures Clery Notice In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act , the University Police department at Florida International University provides information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three (3) calendar years. The FIU Annual Security report is available online at: https://police.fiu.edu/download/annual-security-fire-safety-report/ . To obtain a paper copy of the report, please visit the FIU Police Department located at 885 SW 109th Avenue, Miami, FL, 33199 (PG5 Market Station). Pay Transparency Florida International University will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to 