      "title": "Program Manager - College of Business",
      "description": "Posted Date: 2026-10-28 Department: COB Chapman Graduate School College: College of Business Job family: Administrative Location: Modesto A. Maidique Campus About FIU Florida International University is a Top 50, preeminent public research university with 55,000 students from all 50 states and more than 140 countries, as well as an alumni network of more than 340,000. Located in the global city of Miami, the university offers more than 200 degree programs at the undergraduate, graduate and professional levels, including medicine and law. FIU faculty are leaders in their fields and include National Academy members, Fulbright Scholars and MacArthur Genius Fellows. A Carnegie R1 institution, FIU drives impactful research in environmental resilience, health and technology and innovation. Home to the Wall of Wind and Institute of Environment, FIU stands at the forefront of discovery and innovation. With a focus on student success, economic mobility and community engagement, FIU is redefining what it means to be a public research university. Job Summary Oversees the operations and logistics of the College of Business' Specialized Masters programs. Manages the recruitment, admissions, student and alumni services, and external partnerships. Participates in the development and leads in the implementation of program strategy for the Specialized Masters programs. Oversees the student recruitment and application process that includes reviewing applications to recommend for admission. Oversees the delivery of student services, including orientation, speaker visits, graduation, and special events. Coordinates communication with Specialized Masters programs advisory board. Develops program information to prospective students through various mediums throughout the application and admissions process. Collaborates with departmental leadership in identifying and promoting program initiatives and executes strategies to meet admissions goals. Works closely with Specialized Masters programs leadership to resolve student conflicts and ensure academic integrity as needed. Assists in the engagement of the alumni network and the advisory board. Serves as the University's credit card user for departmental transactions. Adheres to University's rules and regulations. Collaborates with FIU Online and the Specialized Masters programs recruiters on recruitment and marketing efforts. Supervises, develops and coordinates the activities of direct reports. Works closely with the College's Finance and Administration team in the development and management of the program operating budgets. Generates monthly variance reports, and analyzes current and past budgets to develop short and long-term forecast. Approves requisitions and receives goods or services against purchase orders. Oversees travel related requests and expenses. Manages and reconciles program expenses. Collaborates with the Specialized Masters programs Recruiters and College's Marketing and Communications team in developing digital and print promotional collateral's in alignment with program marketing strategy. Interprets University administrative and fiscal policies and procedures. Provides recommendations on procedures for the unit to improve administrative and fiscal operation for the programs and office site. Develops domestic and overseas corporate partnerships. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in an appropriate specialization and four (4) years of related experience, or Master's degree in an appropriate specialization and two (2) years related experience. Desired Qualifications Experience working with PeopleSoft, Canvas, Salesforce, Adobe Connect, Customer Relationship Management software (CRM) and/or ImageNow applications preferred. Experience in recruitment and/or prospect development. Supervisory experience. Job Category Administrative Advertised Salary $50,000 - $60,000 Work Schedule Begin time: 8:30 AM End time: 5:00 PM Pre-Employment Requirements Expanded Background Check Other Information Ability to travel locally and nationally. Ability to travel internationally. Ability to work flexible hours as needed. Ability to work occasional evenings, weekends and at locations outside of the University Travel to FIU Campus How To Apply Current Employee As a current employee, you must log into Employee Self Service (ESS) to apply for this and any other internal career opportunity of interest. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume/ curriculum vitae, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. *This posting will close at 12:00 am of the close date. How To Apply Prospective Employee If you have not created a registered account, you will be asked to create a username and password for use of the system. It is recommended that you provide an active/valid e-mail account as that will be the main source of communication regarding your status within the process. In this account, you are able to track your applicant status in \" My Applications \". To be considered eligible for the position as an internal candidate, departmental staff must meet minimum requirements of the position and be in good performance standing. Before you begin the process, we recommend that you are prepared to attach electronic copies of your resume, cover letter or any other documents within the application process. It is recommended that you combine your cover letter and resume/curriculum vitae into one attachment. Attached documents should be in Microsoft Word or PDF format. 