Department will have the following duties and responsibilities: -Help with creating or updating course materials, including syllabi, reading lists, and lecture slides. -Oversee the online learning platform for the course, ensuring that all non-content-related materials such as syllabi, schedules, and administrative announcements are kept current. -Help coordinate student involvement in academic conferences, including abstract submissions. -Help with the operational aspects of student course improvement assessments such as sending student surveys about the course mid-term, setting up questionnaires online or gather qualitative feedback making sure the instructor and students are kept informed about the results. -Assist with announcement reminders such as deadlines and submission processes -Assist with program admissions related operations Disclosures Clery Notice In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Crime Statistics Act , the University Police department at Florida International University provides information on crimes statistics, crime prevention, law enforcement, crime reporting, and other related issues for the past three (3) calendar years. The FIU Annual Security report is available online at: https://police.fiu.edu/download/annual-security-fire-safety-report/ . To obtain a paper copy of the report, please visit the FIU Police Department located at 885 SW 109th Avenue, Miami, FL, 33199 (PG5 Market Station). Pay Transparency Florida International University will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation inform